hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4201","4195 - Ali ibn Abdillah al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Harith al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr upon his mount. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus, nor from Yunus except Abdillah ibn al-Harith; Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus was alone in transmitting it."
"4202","4196 - Ali ibn Abdillah al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: Idris ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Rabab al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Said ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from his father, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, he said: I suffered severe hardship and distress from prostatic fluid, and would bathe often because of it. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Ablution suffices you for it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about what gets on my garment from it? He said: A handful of water with which you sprinkle your garment where you see it hit suffices you."
"4203","4197 - Ali ibn Abdillah al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: Idris ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Rabab narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Harun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Sahlah bint Suhayl, while she had prolonged bleeding, to bathe for every prayer; that was hard upon her, so he commanded her to combine Zhuhr and Asr in one bath, Maghrib and Isha in one bath, and to bathe for dawn. Al-Ala ibn Harun is the brother of Yazid ibn Harun. No one narrated these two hadiths from him except Asbat ibn Abd al-Wahid; Idris ibn Abi al-Rabab al-Ramli was alone in transmitting them both."
"4204","4198 - Ali ibn Abdillah al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Uthman Abu Hassan al-Ziyadi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Nothing put in my scale is weightier than good character. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Muhayriz except Abu Qilabah, nor from Abu Qilabah except Khalid al-Hadhdha, nor from Khalid except Yazid ibn Zuray; Abu Hassan al-Ziyadi was alone in transmitting it."
"4205","4199 - Ali ibn Abdillah al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: Abu Hassan al-Ziyadi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I never prayed behind an imam whose prayer was more complete nor more concise than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari."
"4206","Ali ibn Abdillah al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: Abu Hassan az-Ziyadi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Talhah, from Umm Sulaym, she said: When the prohibition of wine came down, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a caller to call out: Verily wine has been forbidden, so do not sell it and do not buy it, and whoever has any of it with him, let him pour it away. Abu Talhah said: O boy, untie the waterskin and pour it out. So the people poured it out, and they had no wine on that day except (made from) unripe dates and ripe dates. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari."
"4207","Ali ibn Abdillah al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: Abu Hassan az-Ziyadi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn Urwah ibn az-Zubayr, from his father, from Aishah, she said: A group of Sudanese played in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I was looking between his shoulder and his head. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Urwah except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, and no one narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi."
"4208","Ali ibn Abdillah al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Musa al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Humayd at-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily Allah has barred repentance from the follower of every innovation."
"4209","Ali ibn Abdillah al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: Abu Hassan az-Ziyadi narrated to us, he said: Sawwar ibn Musab narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Abu al-Jahm, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by some food and put his hand into it, then said: Whoever cheats us is not of us. No one narrated this hadith from Mutarrif except Sawwar ibn Musab, and it is not narrated from al-Bara except with this chain."
"4210","Ali ibn Abdillah al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Musa al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two groups of my ummah will not come to me at the Pond and will not enter Paradise: the Qadariyyah and the Murjiah."
"4211","Ali ibn Abdillah al-Farghani narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Musa al-Farwi narrated to us, he said: Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Qadariyyah and the Murjiah are the Magians of this ummah; if they fall sick do not visit them, and if they die do not attend their funerals. No one narrated these two hadiths from Humayd at-Tawil except Anas ibn Iyad; Harun ibn Musa al-Farwi alone narrated them."
"4212","Ali ibn Ahmad Bistam az-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: My uncle Ibrahim ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud at-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Amr ibn Taghlib: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon and said: Amma badu (To proceed). No one narrated this hadith from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz except Abu Dawud; Ibrahim ibn Bistam alone narrated it."
"4213","Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Talut ibn Abbad as-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Ismail al-Kahhal narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Aws, from Buraydah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give glad tidings to those who walk to the mosques in darkness of complete light on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith is not narrated from Buraydah except with this chain; Ismail al-Kahhal alone narrated it."
"4214","Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Khuzai al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Dawud ibn Dalhat narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father Dalhat, from his father Ismail, from his father, that his father Musri ibn Yasir narrated to him, from Amr ibn Murrah al-Juhani, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves that men stand before him should take his seat in the Fire. This hadith is not narrated from Amr ibn Murrah al-Juhani except with this chain."
"4215","Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Abdullah ibn Musa ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to me, he said: My father Abdullah ibn Musa narrated to me, from his father Musa ibn Abdullah, from his father Abdullah ibn al-Hasan, from his father al-Hasan ibn al-Hasan, from his father al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Preserve my regard concerning al-Abbas, for he is the remnant of my forefathers. This hadith is not narrated from al-Hasan ibn Ali except with this chain."
"4216","Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Marruzi narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from al-Mutim ibn al-Miqdam, from Aban ibn Abi Ayyash, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who wakes in the night and says: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, and praise be to Allah, and glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; O Allah, forgive me, except that he is forgiven; then if he resolves and stands and performs ablution and supplicates to Allah, He answers him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mutim ibn al-Miqdam except Yazid ibn Yusuf; Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim alone narrated it."
"4217","Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Mubarak al-Bazzaz as-Susi al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Mahmud ibn Khalid ad-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Ali an-Numayri narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Amr, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Said ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The women of Quraysh are the best women who ride camels: most tender to a child, and most careful with a husband regarding his means. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Amr except Ahmad ibn Ali an-Numayri; Mahmud ibn Khalid alone narrated it."
"4218","Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Mubarak as-Susi narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Ubayd al-Hazza narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Shuayb ibn Abi al-Ashath, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Disputation about the Quran is disbelief. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Shuayb ibn Abi al-Ashath; Muhammad ibn Himyar alone narrated it."
"4219","Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Sulayman an-Naysaburi narrated to us in Baghdad, he said: ar-Rabi ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Mihran, from Abdul Wahid ibn Zayd, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, he said: I entered upon Shaddad ibn Aws while he was weeping, so I said: What makes you weep? He said: Two hadiths I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: What are they? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, and I saw something in his face that distressed me, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this that I see in your face? He said: Two matters I fear for my ummah after me: shirk and hidden desire. Indeed they will not worship a sun, nor a moon, nor an idol, but they will show off with their deeds. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is this shirk? He said: Yes. I said: And what is hidden desire? He said: A man wakes up fasting, then a desire from his desires presents itself to him, so he follows it and abandons the fast. At-Tabarani said: And the explanation of hidden desire is: from what does not please Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"4220","Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Amr al-Qaysi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub as-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a young man came upon us from the mountain pass; when we cast our eyes at him we said: If only this youth would devote his energy and youth and strength in the path of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard our saying and said: And what is the path of Allah except one who is killed? Whoever strives for his parents is in the path of Allah, and whoever strives for his dependents is in the path of Allah, and whoever strives to accumulate is in the path of the Taghut. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Sirin except Ayyub, and no one narrated it from Ayyub except Rabah ibn Amr al-Qaysi; it is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Yunus alone narrated it."
"4221","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Quba, and he was brought a small cup from one of their houses; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his hand in, but the cup could not contain it, so he put in his four fingers and could not put in his thumb. Then he said to the people: Come to the drink. Anas said: My eye saw water gushing from between his fingers, and he did not return the cup until they all drank their fill from it. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways alone narrated it."
"4222","Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Thabit, from Anas, from Abu Talhah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten blessings upon him. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways alone narrated it."
"4223","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, from Ibn Abbas, that a questioner asked him and said: O Abu al-Abbas, does a murderer have repentance? Ibn Abbas said, as if amazed at his affair: What are you saying? He repeated his question to him, and he said to him: What are you saying? Two or three times. Then Ibn Abbas said: How can he have repentance? I heard your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The slain will come holding his head with one of his hands, seizing his killer with his other hand, his jugular veins spurting blood, until he brings him to the Throne; the slain will say to the Lord of the worlds: This one killed me? And Allah will say to the killer: May you be wretched, and he will be taken to the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl except Abu Uways; his son Ismail alone narrated it."
"4224","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Abdur Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us, he said: ar-Rabi ibn Badr narrated to us, he said: an-Nahhas ibn Qahm narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No marriage is valid except with a guardian and two witnesses, and a dowry, whether small or large. No one narrated this hadith from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, except an-Nahhas ibn Qahm, and no one narrated it from an-Nahhas except ar-Rabi and Abdur Rahman ibn Qays ad-Dabbi."
"4225","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Huraym ibn Uthman ar-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: Suwayd Abu Hatim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Musa ibn Salamah, from Ibn Abbas, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I perform Hajj on behalf of my mother, for she has died? He said: Tell me, if she had a debt and you paid it, would it not have been accepted from you? She said: Yes. So he ordered her to perform Hajj on her behalf. And a woman came and said: Shall I make my son perform Hajj while he is nursing or small? He said: Yes. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Suwayd Abu Hatim; Huraym ibn Uthman alone narrated it."
"4226","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr and Talq ibn Habib and Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed three Umrahs in Dhu al-Qadah: one of them from al-Hudaybiyah, and another during the truce with Quraysh, and another upon his return from Khaybar, from al-Jiranah. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr and Talq ibn Habib, except Wuhayb; Sahl ibn Bakkar alone narrated it."
"4227","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid az-Zanji narrated to us, from Abdur Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Madini, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The flank is a vein of the kidney; when it moves it harms its owner, so treat it with burnt water and honey. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Abdur Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Madini; Muslim ibn Khalid az-Zanji alone narrated it."
"4228","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdur Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily I seek Allah's forgiveness in the day and repent to Him seventy times. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdur Rahman, except Ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah, and no one narrated it from them except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways alone narrated it."
"4229","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Juwayriyah ibn Muhammad, the freedman of Bilal ibn Abi Burdah, from whom Hammad ibn Zayd used to narrate, narrated to us, he said: I heard Salim al-Bunani, he said: My master Abu Hani narrated to me, from Umm Hani, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me and I said: O Prophet of Allah, teach me a deed I can do while sitting, for standing has become hard for me. He said: O Umm Hani. I said: At your service, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Glorify Allah one hundred times, for it equals one hundred freed necks; and praise Allah one hundred times, for it equals one hundred horses with their gear in the path of Allah; and magnify Allah one hundred times, for it equals one hundred adorned, let-loose sacrificial camels; and declare Allah's oneness one hundred times, for it does not pass over a sin without wiping it away. No one narrated this hadith from Salim al-Bunani except Juwayriyah ibn Muhammad, and he is Juwayriyah ibn Bashir; Musa ibn Ismail alone narrated it."
"4230","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: While a man was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his camel, he cursed it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not travel with us on a cursed camel. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik ibn Abi Namir except Abu Uways; Ismail alone narrated it."
"4231","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ayyash ibn al-Walid ar-Raqqam narrated to us, he said: Abdul Ala narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Yazid al-Madini, from Anas ibn Malik: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah at Sarif, and consummated the marriage with her at Sarif, and she died at Sarif. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Yazid al-Madini except Qurrah, and no one narrated it from Qurrah except Abdul Ala; Ayyash ar-Raqqam alone narrated it."
"4232","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be matters and trials after me; the best of people in them is the hidden, God-fearing believer. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir except Abu Uways; Ismail alone narrated it."
"4233","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid at-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn ar-Rabi narrated to us, from Umayr ibn Abdullah, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing women and children, and said: They belong to the victor. No one narrated this hadith from Umayr ibn Abdullah except Qays ibn ar-Rabi; Abu al-Walid alone narrated it."
"4234","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily Allah accepts charity and nurtures it for one of you as one of you raises his foal or his young camel. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Abu Uways; his son Ismail alone narrated it."
"4235","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is given a life-grant (umra), it is his and his descendants'. No one narrated this hadith from Yaqub ibn Ata except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Ahmad ibn Yunus alone narrated it."
"4236","Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A fire will come out whose light will illuminate the necks of camels at Busra. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways alone narrated it."
"4237","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from ash-Shabi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has forbidden. No one narrated this hadith from Asim ibn Bahdalah except Aban ibn Yazid; Musa ibn Ismail alone narrated it."
"4238","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Abdur Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us, he said: al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman an-Numayri narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield from the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Kab except Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Rabiah; Fudayl ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"4239","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ayyash ibn al-Walid ar-Raqqam narrated to us, he said: Abdul Ala narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Budayl ibn Maysarah narrated to us, he said: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, he said: Abu Malik al-Ashari said: Shall I not pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he called for water for ablution and performed ablution, then stood for prayer; he lined up men and placed boys behind them. He would say takbir when he prostrated, when he raised his head, and when he stood from the two rakahs, and he gave salam to his right and to his left. No one narrated this hadith from Qurrah except Abdul Ala; Ayyash ibn al-Walid ar-Raqqam alone narrated it."
"4240","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the barber and said: Here. So he shaved his head, and he gave it to Abu Talhah; then he shaved the other side and said: Divide it among the people. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Abbad ibn al-Awwam; Said ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"4241","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Abdur Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform qunut? He said: Yes, briefly after bowing. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal; Abdur Rahman ibn al-Mubarak alone narrated it."
"4242","Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Said, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me, he said: Abu Salamah and Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Abdullah al-Agharr narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The early comer to Friday is like one who offers a camel, then like one who offers a cow, then like one who offers a ram, then like one who offers a chicken, and I think he said: like one who offers an egg. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways alone narrated it."
"4243","Al-Abbas ibn ar-Rabi ibn Thalab narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uqbah ibn Abi al-Ayzar narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid al-Hamdani, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer in congregation exceeds a man's prayer alone by twenty-odd degrees. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid except Yahya ibn Uqbah; ar-Rabi ibn Thalab alone narrated it."
"4244","Al-Abbas ibn ar-Rabi ibn Thalab narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uqbah ibn Abi al-Ayzar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa ibn Abdur Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Mujammi ibn Yahya, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: I went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the market of al-Baqi; he put his hand into a sack and brought out varied food, or he said: adulterated food. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cheats us is not of us. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Mujammi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, except Yahya ibn Uqbah; ar-Rabi ibn Thalab alone narrated it. And Sharik and Qays ibn ar-Rabi narrated it from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Jumay ibn Umayr, from Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, and that is the correct version."
"4245","Al-Abbas ibn ar-Rabi ibn Thalab narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Maysarah, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What makes one of you feel safe, when he raises his head before the imam, from Allah turning his head into the head of a dog. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Maysarah except Abu Ismail al-Muaddib; ar-Rabi ibn Thalab alone narrated it."
"4246","Al-Abbas ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Aqil al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Said al-Muaddib narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims and Allah intends good for him, He provides him a righteous minister; if he forgets, he reminds him, and if he remembers, he helps him. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Abu Said al-Muaddib Faraj ibn Fadalah, from Abu Said; Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim alone narrated it."
"4247","Al-Abbas ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Aqil narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Hurayth al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Musa as-Sinani narrated to us, from Ubaydah ad-Dabbi, from Abu Malik al-Ansari, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Kab ibn Ujrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship or eases for him, Allah will shade him in His shade on a day when there is no shade but His shade. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydah except al-Fadl ibn Musa, and it is not narrated from Kab ibn Ujrah except with this chain."
"4248","Al-Abbas ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Aqil narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from ash-Shabi, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to me, and I said: I have no aversion to you, O Messenger of Allah, but I do not like to marry while my children are small. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women who ride camels are the women of Quraysh: most tender to a child in his childhood, and most careful with a husband regarding his means. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Abu Ismail al-Muaddib."
"4249","Al-Abbas ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Aqil narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Yaqub, from as-Saib ibn Yazid, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take out Abdullah ibn Khatal from beneath the curtains of the Kabah and kill him, then he said: No Qurashi shall be killed after this in captivity. No one narrated this hadith from as-Saib ibn Yazid except Yusuf ibn Yaqub; Abu Mashar alone narrated it."
"4250","Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashii al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Abdur Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umrah three times before his Hajj, in Dhu al-Qadah."
"4251","Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashii narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Abdur Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Umar, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How is the division of the grandfather (in inheritance)? He said: Why do you ask about that, O Umar? I think you will die before you learn that. So he died before learning that. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ibn Harmalah except Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal."
"4252","Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashii narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Huzali narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: I used to pass by this verse: {in the evening and the morning} without knowing what it was, until Umm Hani bint Abi Talib narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her and called for water for ablution in a large bowl, as if I am looking at the trace of dough in it; he performed ablution, then stood and prayed Duha, then said: O Umm Hani, it is the Ishraq prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, except Abu Bakr al-Huzali; Hajjaj ibn Nusayr alone narrated it."
"4253","Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashii narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim as-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning a woman who has a husband and has wealth, and he does not permit her to perform Hajj? He said: She may not go except with her husband's permission. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Ibrahim as-Saigh, and no one narrated it from Ibrahim except Hassan ibn Ibrahim; Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani alone narrated it."
"4254","Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashii narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have left you behind to be my successor among my family. He said: Shall I stay behind after you, O Prophet of Allah? He said: Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me? No one narrated it from Said ibn Abi Arubah except Yazid ibn Zuray, and no one narrated it from Yazid except Ibn Abi Yaqub. And Mamar narrated it from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Sad; and Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated it from Harb ibn Shaddad, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, as Mamar narrated it."
"4255","Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashii narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: We, the company of prophets, were commanded to hasten breaking the fast, to delay the predawn meal, and to place our right hands over our left. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Uyaynah except Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub."
"4256","Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Abbas al-Misri narrated to us in Egypt, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his brother Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning al-Marwah: This is the place of sacrifice, and all the passes of Makkah and its roads are places of sacrifice in Umrah. No one narrated it from Ubaydullah except his brother Abdullah ibn Umar."
"4257","Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abi al-Waddah narrated to us, he said: Salim al-Aftas narrated to us, he said: Razin al-Jurjani narrated to me, he said: I asked Said ibn Jubayr about this verse: {and married women} He said: I have no knowledge of it. So I asked ad-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, and mentioned to him the saying of Said ibn Jubayr. He said: I bear witness that I heard him ask Ibn Abbas about it, and Ibn Abbas said: It was revealed on the day of Khaybar; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, the Muslims took women from among the women of the People of the Book who had husbands; when a man wanted to approach one of them, she would say: I have a husband. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about that, and this verse was revealed: {and married women}, the verse, meaning: captives from among the polytheists may be taken; there is no harm in that. So I mentioned that to Said ibn Jubayr, and he said: ad-Dahhak spoke the truth. No one narrated it from Salim al-Aftas except Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abi al-Waddah."
"4258","Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn al-Faraj Abu Yala ar-Rukhkhi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Mihran ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from as-Suddi, from Rifaah al-Qitbani, from Amr ibn al-Hamiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants a man security over his blood and then kills him, I am free of the killer, even if the slain is a disbeliever. No one narrated it from Ali ibn Abd al-Ala except Mihran."
"4259","Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, ad-Dimashqi, narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abdul Aziz ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from al-Mughirah ibn Hakim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the hypocrite is like a stray sheep between two flocks; when it comes to one, it butts it, and when it comes to the other, it butts it. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym except Abdul Aziz ibn al-Husayn; al-Walid alone narrated it."
"4260","Al-Abbas ibn Ibrahim al-Qaratis narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bakkai narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him wash. No one narrated it from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad except Ziyad al-Bakkai, and Yazid narrated from Nafi nothing but this."
"4261","Al-Abbas ibn Ibrahim al-Qaratis narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Hatim al-Allaf narrated to us, he said: Abdul Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Sulayman at-Taymi narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of you are shepherds, and all of you are responsible for your flocks. No one narrated it from Sulayman except Abdul Wahhab, and no one narrated it from Abdul Wahhab except Ishaq ibn Hatim."
"4262","Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Asbahani al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, he said: My brother Husayn ibn Abi Yazid narrated to us, from Qays ibn ar-Rabi, from Said ibn Masruq, from Abu ad-Duha, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice, and we chose him, and he did not count it as anything. No one narrated it from Said ibn Masruq except Qays, and no one narrated it from Qays except Husayn ibn Abi Burdah."
"4263","Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Abi Burdah narrated to us, he said: My brother Husayn narrated to me, from Qays, from Asim ibn Sulayman and Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Two garments and two sales were forbidden: a man wrapping himself in a single garment exposing his private part to the sky, and wrapping over his left side then lifting it; and (sales by) touching and throwing. No one narrated it from Ashath and Asim except Qays ibn ar-Rabi."
"4264","Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa ad-Damaghani narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, raising the hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Among what Allah created is a rooster whose claws are on the seventh earth and whose comb is folded beneath the Throne, its two wings at the two horizons; when the last third of the night remains, it beats its wings, then says: Glory be to the Sovereign, the Holy; glory be to our Lord, the Sovereign, the Holy; we have no god other than Him. Everything between the east and west hears it except the two weighty beings, and people think roosters only beat their wings when they crow because they heard that. No one narrated it from Mansur except Ibn Ishaq, and no one narrated it from Ibn Ishaq except Salamah ibn al-Fadl, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except from this route."
"4265","Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa ad-Damaghani narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Mikal, from Layth, from Ibrahim at-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, was Adam a prophet? He said: Yes, he was a prophet and messenger; Allah spoke to him directly. He said to him: {O Adam, dwell thou and thy wife in the Garden}. No one narrated it from Ibrahim at-Taymi except Layth, and no one narrated it from Layth except Mikal, and he is a Kufan shaykh; we do not know him to have narrated any hadith other than this."
"4266","Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isa ad-Damaghani narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Humran narrated to us, he said: Hisham ad-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on a small mat. No one narrated it from Qatadah except Hisham, and no one narrated it from Hisham except Amr ibn Humran."
"4267","Abu al-Fadl Abbas ibn Hammad ibn Fadalah as-Sayrafi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn al-Faraj ar-Riyashi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Awn narrated to us, from Abdul Malik ibn Zurarah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not bestow upon a servant a blessing in family, wealth, or child, and he says: What Allah wills; there is no power except with Allah, then he sees any affliction in it short of death. And he recited: {And why, when thou entered thy garden, didst thou not say: What Allah wills; there is no power except with Allah}. This hadith is not narrated from Abdul Malik ibn Zurarah, from Anas, except with this chain; Umar ibn Yunus alone narrated it."
"4268","Al-Abbas ibn Hammad ibn Fadalah as-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Fadl al-Khuraqi narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Zamah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who seeks omens by birds or for whom they are sought, or practices soothsaying or has it done for him, or practices augury or has it done for him."
"4269","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you of the people of Paradise? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Every weak, oppressed one with two worn garments, paid no heed to; if he swears by Allah, He fulfills it. Shall I not inform you of the people of the Fire? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Every coarse, rude, arrogant one. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is jazz? He said: The bulky. I said: And what is jaz? He said: The one great in his own self. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Yahya al-Qattat except Israil, and no one narrated it from Mujahid except Abu Yahya al-Qattat."
"4270","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah at-Tinnisi narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Zayd, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Said ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will raise the servants on the Day of Resurrection, then He will distinguish the scholars and say: O company of scholars, I did not place My knowledge in you while intending to punish you; go, for I have forgiven you. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Abi Hind except Musa ibn Ubaydah, and no one narrated it from Musa except Talhah ibn Zayd; Sadaqah ibn Abdullah alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"4271","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Ansari narrated to me, from Salih, the freedman of at-Tawamah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not harm the living by the dead. No one narrated it from Salih, the freedman of at-Tawamah, except Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Ansari; Sadaqah ibn Abdullah alone narrated it."
"4272","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Murrah, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn az-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never given a choice between two matters except that he took the easier of them, so long as it was not a sin; if it was a sin, he was the furthest of people from it. And he never avenged himself for anything done to him until the sanctities of Allah were violated, then he would avenge for Him. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Murrah except Sadaqah ibn Abdullah; Amr ibn Abi Salamah alone narrated it."
"4273","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah at-Tinnisi narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Bathing on Friday is obligatory upon every adult. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Zuhayr ibn Muhammad; Amr ibn Abi Salamah alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"4274","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The orphan girl is consulted about herself, and her silence is her consent. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Ibn Uyaynah; al-Firyabi alone narrated it."
"4275","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj as-Sami narrated to me, he said: Abdul Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hazza, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Snakes are the transformed jinn, just as monkeys and pigs were transformed from Banu Israil."
"4276","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Abdul Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hazza, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn as-Samit, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he mentioned Zamzam: It is blessed; it is food for nourishment. No one narrated these two hadiths from Khalid al-Hazza except Abdul Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar."
"4277","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Abu ar-Rabi az-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The emergence of the signs, some following others, following one another as beads follow one another in a string. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Dawud al-Ataki; Abu ar-Rabi alone narrated it."
"4278","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Sharik, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah and Jabir ibn Abdullah, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Draw near and be upright, for none of you will be saved by his deed. They said: Not even you, O Prophet of Allah? He said: Not even I, except that Allah envelops me with mercy and grace. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Jabir, except Sharik; Hatim ibn Ismail alone narrated it."
"4279","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted az-Zubayr as a land grant the distance his horse runs, in a land called Thurayr; so he made the horse run until it stopped, then he threw his whip and said: Give him up to where the whip reached. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Abdullah ibn Umar; Hammad ibn Khalid alone narrated it."
"4280","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Rabiah al-Kilabi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered in the year of the Conquest from the pass of al-Idhkhir. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim except Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad; Muhammad ibn Rabiah alone narrated it."
"4281","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Kisai al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from his father, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Hudhayfah asked a farmer for drink, so he gave him drink in a vessel of silver; so he threw it at him, then said: Had I not already warned him once or twice, indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to drink from gold and silver, and to wear silk and brocade; for it is for them in this world, and it is for us in the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, and no one narrated it from Fudayl except Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl; Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Kisai alone narrated it."
"4282","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, he said: Abu Mashar al-Barra Yusuf ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from his father, from Abdur Rahman ibn Awf: That he witnessed that, when Uthman ibn Affan gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he equipped the Army of Hardship with; he brought seven hundred uqiyyahs of gold. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Aban ibn Uthman, and no one narrated it from Ibrahim except Abu Mashar; al-Muqaddami alone narrated it."
"4283","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting: al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Layla, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning one in ihram who dies: He is shrouded in his two garments, his head is not covered, no perfume is applied to him, he is washed with water and lote, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting talbiyah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Salih except al-Aswad ibn Amir; Ahmad ibn Hanbal alone narrated it."
"4284","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Humayd ar-Razi narrated to me, he said: Zafir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Uyaynah, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sad, he said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, live as you wish, for you will die; and do as you wish, for you will be recompensed for it; and love whom you wish, for you will part from him; and know that the honor of the believer is standing in night prayer, and his might is his independence of people. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Uyaynah except Zafir, and Muhammad ibn Uyaynah is the brother of Sufyan."
"4285","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to me, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Yunus, from az-Zuhri, he said: Nafi said: Abdullah ibn Umar, when he returned to Madinah, would halt at al-Batha at Dhu al-Hulayfah, where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had halted. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Yunus, and no one narrated it from Yunus except Hassan ibn Ibrahim; al-Azraq ibn Ali alone narrated it."
"4286","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to me, he said: Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from his father, from Urwah ibn az-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I lay across in front of him. No one narrated this hadith from Yaqub ibn Ata except Abu Ismail al-Muaddib; Surayj ibn Yunus alone narrated it."
"4287","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to me, he said: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that Fatimah bint Abi Hubaysh said: O Messenger of Allah, I suffer prolonged bleeding and do not become pure; shall I abandon prayer? He said: That is not menstruation; it is only a vein. When menstruation comes, abandon prayer, and when it goes — or she said: turns away — wash the blood from you and pray. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Ismail ibn Ulayyah."
"4288","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, he said: Abdul Warith narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Raja, from Aws ibn Damaj, from Uqbah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people are led by the earliest of them in emigration; if their emigration is equal, then the oldest; if they are equal in age, then the most reciting (of the Quran). No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Abdul Warith."
"4289","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Abdul Warith ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, she said: We used to garland sheep, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would send them while lawful, not forbidding anything."
"4290","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj as-Sami narrated to us, he said: Abdul Warith ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, and he mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let none of you say: I forgot such-and-such verse, for he did not forget, but was made to forget."
"4291","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Mihran as-Sabbak narrated to us, he said: Abdul Warith ibn Said narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Zubayd, from Ibn Abdur Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform witr with three, reciting in the first: {Glorify the name of thy Lord, the Most High}, in the second: {Say: O disbelievers}, and in the third: {Say: He is Allah, One}. No one narrated these hadiths from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Abdul Warith, and no one said in the witr hadith, from Ibn Abza from Aishah, except Jafar ibn Mihran as-Sabbak."
"4292","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abdullah at-Tirmidhi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Amir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Tawus, he said: I bear witness upon my father Tawus, that he said: I bear witness upon Jabir ibn Abdullah, that he said: I bear witness upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they do that, they have protected their blood and wealth, except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Tawus except his son, and no one narrated it from Ibn Tawus except Sufyan ibn Amir; Salih ibn Abdullah at-Tirmidhi alone narrated it."
"4293","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj as-Sami narrated to me, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, from Abayah ibn Rifah, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I am cowardly and weak. He said: Come to a jihad with no thorns in it: Hajj. This hadith is not narrated from Husayn ibn Ali except with this chain."
"4294","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Huraym ibn Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from Abdur Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died on Monday and was buried on Wednesday night. No one narrated this hadith from Huraym ibn Sufyan except Aswad ibn Amir."
"4295","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us, he said: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Tufayl Abu Sidan al-Absi narrated to us, he said: I heard Shaddad ibn Ammar say: Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come upon my ummah a time when they will wish for the Dajjal. I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, what is that due to? He said: Due to what they meet of hardship and hardship. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd ibn Tufayl except Qabisah; Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii alone narrated it."
"4296","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Thabit ibn al-Walid ibn Abdullah ibn Jumay narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Abu at-Tufayl said to me: I lived through eight years of the life of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I was born in the year of Uhud. Abdullah said: My father said: Thabit ibn al-Walid came to us from Kufah and stayed in the city of Abu Jafar; I went with Yahya ibn Main and we heard hadiths from him."
"4297","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warkani narrated to me, he said: Abu Shihab al-Hannat narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have entered evening and sovereignty belongs to Allah, and praise be to Allah; I seek refuge with Allah who holds the sky lest it fall upon the earth except by His permission, from the evil of what He created, spread, and originated. Whoever says them is protected from every sorcerer, soothsayer, devil, and envier. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Ibn Abi Layla, and no one narrated it from Ibn Abi Layla except Abu Shihab."
"4298","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj as-Sami narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Thumamah ibn Abdullah ibn Anas narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a donkey branded on its face and said: Allah curses whoever did this."
"4299","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj as-Sami narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Thumamah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not remove his sandals in prayer except once; the people removed their sandals, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you remove your sandals? They said: We saw you remove yours, so we removed ours. He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, informed me that there was filth in them. No one narrated these two hadiths from Thumamah except Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna al-Ansari."
"4300","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdur Rahman at-Tufawi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub as-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Musa ibn Salamah, he said: We were with Ibn Abbas in Makkah, and I said: When we are with you we pray four, and when we return to our lodgings we pray two? He said: That is the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Muhammad ibn Abdur Rahman at-Tufawi and al-Harith ibn Umayr."
"4301","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Uways narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Amrah, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in and heard the voice of a boy weeping, and said: What is wrong with this boy of yours weeping? Why do you not seek ruqyah for him against the evil eye? No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr except Abu Uways."
"4302","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abd al-Malik Abu Qudamah al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Aishah bint Sad narrated to us, from Umm Dharrah, she said: I saw Aishah praying Duha, saying: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray except four rakahs. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Dharrah except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Hanbal alone narrated it, may Allah's mercy and pleasure be upon him."
"4303","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Waki narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mujalid, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever disowns his child to disgrace him in this world, Allah will disgrace him on the Day of Resurrection before all witnesses, requital for requital. No one narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mujalid; Waki alone narrated it."
"4304","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to me, he said: Malik ibn Suayr narrated to us, he said: Furat ibn Ahnaf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ribi ibn Hirash, that Ali ibn Abi Talib stood as a preacher in ar-Rahbah; he praised Allah and extolled Him as He deserves, then said what Allah willed him to say, then called for a cup of Zamzam water; he rinsed from it, wiped, and drank the remainder of his ablution water while standing, then said: I have heard that a man among you dislikes drinking while standing; this is the ablution of one who has not broken it, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do likewise. No one narrated this hadith from Ribi except Ahnaf Abu Furat; Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad alone narrated it."
"4305","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Salim ash-Shashi narrated to me, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Uqbah ibn Aws, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: How will you be when you remain among the dregs of people, whose covenants and trusts have become confused, and they differ and become like this? And he interlaced his fingers. They said: How is the way out, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Take what you know, leave what you reject, attend to your own self, and beware of their common folk. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Mamar, and no one narrated it from Mamar except Ubaydullah ibn Amr; Isa ibn Salim alone narrated it."
"4306","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Khalid al-Khayyat narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Khalid, from Atiyyah ibn al-Harith, from Humayd al-Azraq, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it: {Indeed, it is work unrighteous}. This hadith is not narrated from Masruq except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn Dinar alone narrated it."
"4307","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Aban narrated to me, he said: Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to wipe over the two leather socks, even if one of us comes from relieving himself. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah ibn Ammar except Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid; Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban alone narrated it."
"4308","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi ar-Rabi as-Samman narrated to me, he said: al-Harith ibn Nabhan narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn as-Saib narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Anas ibn Malik, that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said that she had committed adultery, and she was pregnant. He said: Go until you deliver your burden; had she not returned to him, he would not have sent for her. So she delivered her burden, then came to him, and he said: Go until you wean your child. So she came to him, and had she not come to him, he would not have sent for her; she came after she had weaned him, and he stoned her. No one narrated this hadith from Bakr ibn Abdullah except with this chain; Said ibn Abi ar-Rabi as-Samman alone narrated it."
"4309","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Abu Mamar al-Qatii narrated to me, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Abu Janab al-Kalbi, from Maghra, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever hears the call and does not answer without an excuse, he has no prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Maghra except Abu Janab, and no one narrated it from Abu Janab except Jarir; Abu Mamar alone narrated it."
"4310","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jarawi narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah and Ibn Awn, from Ibrahim, from Abdur Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Masud: That he stoned the Jamrah from the bottom of the valley, then said: This is the station of the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was revealed. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Hushaym; Yahya ibn Hassan alone narrated it."
"4311","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Faid narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Ubayd as-Sammak narrated to us, he said: I heard Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani say: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah said: O son of Adam, if thy sins reach the clouds of the sky then thou seek My forgiveness, I will forgive thee and I do not care. O son of Adam, if thou come to Me with earthful of sins then meet Me associating nothing with Me, I will come to thee with its like of forgiveness. No one narrated this hadith from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani except Said ibn Ubayd, and no one narrated it from Said except Kathir ibn Faid; Abu Asim alone narrated it."
"4312","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Burayd ibn Abi Burdah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When Allah intends mercy for a nation among His servants, He takes its prophet before it and makes him a predecessor and forerunner before it; and when He intends its destruction, He punishes it while its prophet is alive and watching, so He delights his eye by its destruction when they denied him and disobeyed his command. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain; al-Qawariri alone narrated it."
"4313","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Maruf narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Aban ibn Salih, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Ali, he said: Slaves from the people of Makkah went out to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of al-Hudaybiyah before dawn and embraced Islam; their masters from Makkah sent to him: By Allah, O Muhammad, they did not come out to thee out of desire for thy religion, but they came out fleeing from slavery. Some men among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah; return them to them. So he became angry, then said: I do not see you, O company of Quraysh, desisting until Allah sends upon you one who strikes your necks for this religion. And he refused to return them and said: They are the freedmen of Allah. And others came out after the truce, and he returned them. No one narrated this hadith from Aban ibn Salih except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Muhammad ibn Salamah alone narrated it."
"4314","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Abu Mamar Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to me, he said: Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to me, from Umarah, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows a funeral from its family until prayer is offered over it, he has a qirat; and whoever follows it until it is buried, he has two qirats, the smaller of which is like Uhud. No one narrated this hadith from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah except Ubaydah ibn Humayd."
"4315","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya ar-Riqashi al-Khazzaz narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in prayer over the dead: O Allah, forgive him, send blessings upon him, bless him, and bring him to the Pond of Thy Messenger. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Ayyub, and no one narrated it from Ayyub except Asim ibn Hilal; Zakariyya ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"4316","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Muhammad at-Talhi narrated to me, he said: Dawud ibn Ata al-Muzani narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ubayy ibn Kab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first whom the Truth shakes hands with is Umar, and the first whom He takes by his hand and admits to Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Salih ibn Kaysan and Umar ibn Qays."
"4317","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Ibn Hurmuz al-Araj narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar. This hadith is not narrated from Muawiyah except with this chain; Yaqub ibn Ibrahim alone narrated it."
"4318","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Aban ibn Salih, from Qusaym, the freedman of Umarah, from Qazah ibn Yahya, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Saddles are not tied except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Furthest Mosque, and my mosque. No one narrated this hadith from Qusaym except Aban ibn Salih, and no one narrated it from Aban except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Yaqub ibn Ibrahim alone narrated it."
"4319","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas, he said: I came to him — meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — while he wore a striped cloak, in a garden, branding the camels. He said: Gently. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Ibn Abi Adi and Hatim ibn Wardan; Abu Kamil al-Jahdari alone narrated it from Hatim ibn Wardan."
"4320","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Ashqar narrated to us, he said: Jafar al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Mikhwal, from Mundhir ath-Thawri, from Umm Salamah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry, none dared speak to him except Ali. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this chain; Husayn al-Ashqar alone narrated it."
"4321","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Aban narrated to me, he said: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, from Jarir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For the traveler three (days), and for the resident a day, concerning wiping over the leather socks. No one narrated this hadith from Talhah ibn Musarrif except al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, and no one narrated it from al-Qasim except Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad; Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban alone narrated it."
"4322","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to me, he said: Abu Said al-Muaddib narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, from ash-Shabi, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: I have not forgotten, among what I forgot of things, the greeting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer to his right and left: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah except Abu Said al-Muaddib; Mansur alone narrated it."
"4323","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Main narrated to me, he said: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Evil is the mountain pass, Jiyad. He said it twice or thrice. They said: Why is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The Beast will emerge and scream three screams, and whatever is between the east and west will hear it. No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih except Rabah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Umar, and no one narrated it from Rabah except Hisham ibn Yusuf; Yahya ibn Main alone narrated it."
"4324","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Abu Mamar al-Qatii narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken, there befell my father what, had it befallen firm mountains, would have crushed them: disbelief appeared and hypocrisy raised its head. They did not differ over a single point except that my father flew to its merit and excellence. He said: And she would mention Umar ibn al-Khattab and say: By Allah, he was keen and unique, having prepared for affairs their peers. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Abdullah ibn Jafar; Abu Mamar alone narrated it."
"4325","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj as-Sami narrated to me, he said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Mamar, from az-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are but like a hundred camels, among which no mount is found. Thus Mamar narrated it in Basrah; and he narrated it in Sanaa from az-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, and that is the correct version."
"4326","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from az-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abdur Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw spittle in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it, then said: When one of you spits, let him not spit toward the qiblah; let him spit to his left. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Hassan ibn Ibrahim; Muhammad ibn Bakkar alone narrated it."
"4327","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, he heard it from Said ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and Muadh to Yemen and said to them: Make easy, give glad tidings, teach, and do not repel. When they turned to go, Abu Musa returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, they have a drink of honey cooked until it thickens, and mizr made from barley? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything that intoxicates, keeping from prayer, is forbidden. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah; Muhammad ibn Abbad alone narrated it."
"4328","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Imran narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn al-Husayn, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience to a creature in disobedience to Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Simak ibn Harb except Hafs ibn Imran; Ismail ibn Aban alone narrated it."
"4329","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to me, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Amir ibn Shaqiq, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, he said: I watched the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not stop the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrat al-Aqabah. No one narrated this hadith from Amir ibn Shaqiq except Sharik; Zahmawayh alone narrated it."
"4330","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to me, he said: Sinan ibn Harun al-Burjumi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi, from Hudhayfah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and I prayed his prayer behind him without his knowing; he began al-Baqarah and read from it until I thought he would bow, then he went on. Sufyan said: I know only that he said: He prayed four rakahs; his bowing was like his standing. He said: I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Why didst thou not inform me. Hudhayfah said: By Him who sent thee with the truth as a prophet, I still feel it in my back to this hour. He said: Had I known thou wert behind me, I would have lightened. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Sinan ibn Harun; Zahmawayh alone narrated it."
"4331","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Huraym ibn Abd al-Ala Abu Hamzah al-Asadi narrated to me, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrating from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit until he bows two rakahs. None raised this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah; Mutamir alone narrated it."
"4332","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Utbah, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from an-Numan ibn Bashir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sleeps intending to pray at night, let him place at his right a handful of dust; when he wakes, let him take some of it with his right and throw it to his left. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Ayyub ibn Utbah; Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid alone narrated it."
"4333","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Durays narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, from al-Hirmas ibn Ziyad, he said: I was riding behind my father, and I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a camel, saying: Labbayk with Hajj and Umrah together."
"4334","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: While I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man came to him, greeted him, then turned away from him. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I love this man. He said: Hast thou informed him? I said: No. He said: Then inform thy brother of that. So I followed him, greeted him, took him by his shoulders, and said: By Allah, I love thee for Allah's sake. He said: By Allah, I love thee for Allah's sake. And I said: Had the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not commanded me to inform thee, I would not have done so. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar and Musa ibn Uqbah except Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, and no one narrated it from Zuhayr except Hassan; al-Azraq ibn Ali alone narrated it."
"4335","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Hadrami Sajjadah narrated to us, he said: Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that a woman used to borrow jewelry in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then keep it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let the woman repent to Allah and to His Messenger, and return what she has. Yet she refused. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Arise, O so-and-so, take her hand and cut it off. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Abu Malik al-Janbi; al-Hasan ibn Hammad alone narrated it."
"4336","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard Ibrahim ibn Sad az-Zuhri in the year one hundred eighty-two say: ar-Rabi ibn Subayh narrated to me, from Abu Uthman, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is forbidden. Abdullah said: My father said: Abu Uthman al-Ansari, his name is Amr ibn Salim. Mahdi ibn Maymun, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, and Mutarrif ibn Tarif narrated it from him. Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Abu Tumaylah narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I saw Abu Uthman al-Ansari Amr ibn Salim judging in a town. My father said: He was a judge in Marw. No one narrated this hadith from ar-Rabi ibn Subayh except Ibrahim ibn Sad; Ahmad ibn Hanbal alone narrated it."
"4337","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: When the illness of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which he was taken came, he said: Call for me Abu Bakr and his son, so that I may write for them a writing, lest one greedy for the affair of Abu Bakr covet it, or one wishing wish for it. Then he said: Allah and the Muslims refuse that — twice. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi ibn Umar except Muammal ibn Ismail."
"4338","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to me, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Adi ibn Thabit except Ashath ibn Sawwar; Sharik alone narrated it."
"4339","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, he said: Humayd ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, he said: ad-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Hakim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I did not toss and turn this night but I heard a voice in the mosque. I said: O Messenger of Allah, that is al-Hawla bint Tuwayt, who does not sleep when people sleep. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked what I said, until I saw that in his face, and he said: Verily Allah does not weary until you weary. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except ad-Dahhak ibn Uthman, and no one narrated it from ad-Dahhak except Humayd ibn al-Aswad; al-Muqaddami alone narrated it."
"4340","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, he said: Hasan ibn Husayn al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Malik al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, he said: I said to Aishah: With what did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform witr? She said: He used to perform witr with {Glorify the name of thy Lord, the Most High} and {Say: O disbelievers} and {Say: He is Allah, One}. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Malik al-Ashjai except Hasan ibn Husayn al-Kufi; al-Muqaddami alone narrated it."
"4341","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Abdullah az-Zubayri narrated to me, he said: Aishah bint al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu az-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday; in it Adam was created, in it he was admitted to Paradise, in it he was taken out of it, and the Hour will not come except on Friday. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Aishah bint al-Mundhir; Muawiyah ibn Abdullah az-Zubayri alone narrated it."
"4342","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Abdullah az-Zubayri narrated to me, he said: Aishah bint al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from az-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, that a woman said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah's ordinance of Hajj has overtaken my father as a very old man who cannot hold onto the mount; shall I perform Hajj on his behalf? He said: Yes. He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of thy father. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Aishah bint al-Mundhir; Muawiyah ibn Abdullah alone narrated it."
"4343","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting: Khalid ibn Nafi al-Ashari narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa, he said: We prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over a funeral, and he gave salam to his right and to his left."
"4344","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Abu Shurahbil Isa ibn Khalid al-Himsi, brother of Abu al-Yaman, narrated to me, he said: My uncle Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named himself names for us, among them what we memorized and among them what we did not memorize. He said: I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, al-Muqaffi, al-Hashir, the Prophet of repentance, and the Prophet of battle. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Ismail ibn Ayyash, and no one narrated it from Ismail except Abu al-Yaman; Abu Shurahbil alone narrated it."
"4345","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Hadiyyah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Marwazi narrated to me, he said: Umar ibn Ubayd at-Tanafisi narrated to us, he said: Abu Sad al-Baqqal narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left us while we were numerous, and there is none of us who searched out a deep wound or a displacing wound, except Umar or Ibn Umar. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Husayn except Abu Sad al-Baqqal; Umar ibn Ubayd alone narrated it."
"4346","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdur Rahman at-Tufawi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Abi Tamimah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a lower garment that rustled. He said: Who is this? I said: Abdullah. He said: If thou art Abdullah, raise thy lower garment to mid-shin. So his lower garment remained so until he died. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Muhammad ibn Abdur Rahman at-Tufawi."
"4347","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to me, he said: Qays ibn ar-Rabi narrated to us, from Salim al-Aftas, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that a man was thrown by his camel and died while in ihram. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him with water and lote, shroud him in his two garments, do not bring perfume near him, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting talbiyah. No one narrated this hadith from Salim al-Aftas except Qays; Muhammad ibn Bakkar alone narrated it."
"4348","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Bakkar al-Barrad al-Himsi narrated to me, he said: ar-Rabi ibn Rawh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abrash narrated to us, from az-Zubaydi Muhammad ibn al-Walid, from Adi ibn Abdur Rahman, and he is Abu al-Haytham ibn Adi, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abdullah ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have acquired land at Khaybar, never acquiring wealth more precious to me than it; what dost thou command? He said: If thou wish, withhold its corpus and give its yield in charity. He said: So Umar withheld its corpus and gave it in charity: not to be sold, nor given away, nor inherited; for the poor, for freeing necks, in the path of Allah, for the wayfarer, and the guest. There is no sin upon whoever administers it to eat from it in a proper manner and to feed a friend, without hoarding wealth therein. This hadith is not narrated from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except with this chain; ar-Rabi ibn Rawh alone narrated it."
"4349","Abdullah ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Jurayj ar-Rahawi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The stomach is the cistern of the body, and the veins come to it; if the stomach is sound, the veins issue with health, and if the stomach is corrupt, the veins issue with sickness. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah; Ibrahim ibn Jurayj ar-Rahawi alone narrated it."
"4350","Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn as-Sari narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Labbayk, God of Truth. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Zakariyya ibn Ishaq, and no one narrated it from Zakariyya except Bishr ibn as-Sari; Marwan ibn Ubayd alone narrated it."
"4351","4345 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Marwan al-Khallal narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: I entered upon Hind bint al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah, the wife of al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf, with a spindle in her hand spinning with it, so I said to her: You spin though you are the wife of a commander? She said: I heard my father narrating from my grandfather, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The longest of you in productive work is the greatest of you in reward. Abu Sufrah did not transmit any hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) other than this, and it is not narrated from him except with this chain; Yazid ibn Marwan is alone in transmitting it, and the name of Abu Sufrah is Sariq ibn Zalim."
"4352","4346 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Marwan al-Khallal narrated to us, he said: al-Yaqzan ibn Umayr narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I heard Ammar ibn Yasir say: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group of his Companions: Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, Muadh, Hudhayfah and Sad, eight years after the Hijrah, in the ninth year, and Hudhayfah asked him: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, tell us about the tribulations. He said: O Hudhayfah, indeed there will come upon my ummah a time in which the one sitting is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking; the killer and the killed are in the Fire. This hadith is not narrated from Ammar ibn Yasir except with this chain."
"4353","4347 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Dawud al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ayyub, Hisham ibn Hassan, Ubaydullah ibn Umar and Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, and from Bakr ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, there is no partner for You, here I am; indeed praise, blessing and dominion belong to You; there is no partner for You. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub, Hisham and Habib except Hammad ibn Salamah; Abd al-Aziz ibn Dawud is alone in transmitting it."
"4354","4348 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led a prayer, either adding to it or omitting from it, so some of the people said to him: Has something new happened in the prayer? He said: Nothing new has happened in it, and if something had happened I would have told you, but I am a human being who forgets, so when I forget remind me. Then he prayed what remained of his prayer, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then said: When one of you prays and does not know whether he added or omitted, let him seek what is most correct, then prostrate two prostrations while sitting. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except al-Harith ibn Umayr; Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb al-Harrani is alone in transmitting it."
"4355","4349 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhajir narrated to me, from Ismail, the freed slave of Abdullah ibn Amr, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the killing of a believer is greater in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection than the passing away of the world. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Muhammad ibn Salamah is alone in transmitting it."
"4356","4350 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Umayr, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, about the fear prayer, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and a group of us stood behind him and prayed behind him, while the other group faced the enemy; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed one rakah with the group with him and two prostrations, then they left to face the enemy, and the group that had not prayed came and prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prayed with them one rakah and two prostrations, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the salam, then each one of the two groups prayed by themselves one rakah and two prostrations. No one raised this hadith from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani except al-Harith ibn Umayr; Musa ibn Ayan is alone in transmitting it."
"4357","4351 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I asked Ubayy ibn Kab about the two Muawwidhatayn, and he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about them, and he said: No one before you asked me about them; it was said to me, so I said. Ubayy said: So it was said to us, and we said."
"4358","4352 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: Ubayy ibn Kab said to me: How many verses do you count Surah al-Ahzab to be? I said: We count it as seventy-two or seventy-three verses. He said: It used to equal Surah al-Baqarah, and in it was: The old man and the old woman, when they commit adultery, stone them as a punishment from Allah, and Allah is Mighty, Wise."
"4359","4353 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ubayy, he said: Laylat al-Qadr is the night of the twenty-seventh. I said: Abu al-Mundhir, how did you know that? He said: By the sign which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us and we memorized. Then he swore without exception, saying: By the One Who sent down the Book upon Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), it is indeed the night of the twenty-seventh."
"4360","4354 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Ishaq, from Wahb ibn Jabir, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It is not fitting for a Muslim to neglect those whom he maintains."
"4361","4355 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever eats dates with a group of people should not pair them, and if he wishes to do so let him ask their permission; if they permit him, let him do so if he wishes."
"4362","4356 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing unripe dates and ripe dates, meaning: to make nabidh from them."
"4363","4357 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, he said: Jundub narrated to us that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) five days before his death say: I have had among you brothers and friends, and I declare myself free before Allah of having had any intimate friend among you; had I taken an intimate friend from my ummah I would have taken Abu Bakr as an intimate friend, but my Lord has taken me as an intimate friend just as He took Ibrahim as an intimate friend. Indeed those before you used to take the graves of their prophets as mosques, and I forbid you from that."
"4364","4358 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Abdullah ibn Rabiah, from Ubayd ibn Khalid, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between two men of his Companions; one of them was killed and the other lived after him as long as Allah willed, then died, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began supplicating for him, and the utmost of their supplication was that Allah join him with his brother who had been killed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of the two do you say is better? They said: The one who was killed. He said: Do you not count the prayer and fasting of this one as merit? What is between them is farther than what is between heaven and earth. So he gave precedence to the one who died over the one who was killed. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah except Ubaydullah ibn Amr."
"4365","4359 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam al-Ghassani narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Muhammad al-Thaqafi, from Bilal ibn Abi al-Darda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your love for a thing blinds and deafens. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam is alone in transmitting it."
"4366","4360 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam al-Ghassani narrated to us, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ill omen is bad character."
"4367","4361 - Abdullah ibn Ayyub al-Qarabi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Dhuhli narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, he said: I came to Makkah and found there Abu Hanifah, Ibn Abi Layla and Ibn Shubrumah. I asked Abu Hanifah, saying: What do you say about a man who makes a sale and stipulates a condition? He said: The sale is void and the condition is void. Then I went to Ibn Abi Layla and asked him, and he said: The sale is valid and the condition is void. Then I went to Ibn Shubrumah and asked him, and he said: The sale is valid and the condition is valid. I said: Glory be to Allah, three jurists of Iraq and you differ with me on one issue. So I went to Abu Hanifah and told him, and he said: I do not know what the two said; Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a sale combined with a condition; the sale is void and the condition is void. Then I went to Ibn Abi Layla and told him, and he said: I do not know what the two said; Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to buy Barirah and free her; the sale is valid and the condition is void. Then I went to Ibn Shubrumah and told him, and he said: I do not know what the two said; Misar ibn Kidam narrated to me, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I sold a she-camel to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and stipulated carrying me on it to Madinah; the sale is valid and the condition is valid. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hanifah, Ibn Abi Layla and Ibn Shubrumah except Abd al-Warith."
"4368","4362 - Abdullah ibn Ayyub al-Qarabi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Sad al-Yamami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married together with her paternal aunt, nor with her maternal aunt. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Mubarak ibn Sad al-Yamami, and no one included Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan between Sulayman ibn Yasar and Abu Hurayrah except Yahya ibn Abi Kathir."
"4369","4363 - Abdullah ibn Ayyub al-Qarabi narrated to us, he said: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Rawh al-Qasim, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor and the muadhdhin is trusted; O Allah, forgive the muadhdhins and guide the imams."
"4370","4364 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from Abu Yahya al-Qattat, from Mujahid, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The key to Paradise is prayer, and the key to prayer is ablution."
"4371","4365 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, he said: Abu Malik al-Nakhai narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying to another: O Shahanshah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is the King of kings. No one narrated this hadith from Asim al-Ahwal except Abu Malik; Adam is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"4372","4366 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan al-Rahawi narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah say: I heard Mujahid say: I heard Said ibn al-Musayyib say: I heard Suhayb say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: He has not believed in the Quran who deems its prohibitions lawful. This hadith is not narrated from Suhayb except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan is alone in transmitting it."
"4373","4367 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Kabshah al-Anmari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah is of four kinds: a man given wealth who spends it in obedience to Allah, and a man sees him and says: If I had wealth like his I would do with it as he did, so they are equal in reward; and a man given wealth who squanders it and corrupts it, and a man sees him and says: If I had like this I would do with it as he did, so they are equal in sin."
"4374","4368 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever supplicates with a supplication in which there is no sin nor severing of kinship, Allah gives him through it one of three: either He forgives him a past sin through it, or He hastens it for him in this world, or He stores it for him in the Hereafter."
"4375","4369 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Said, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Khawarij, he said: Their likeness is that of a man who shot an arrow, and the arrow went far to where it landed, so he took it and looked at its feathers and saw on it neither grease nor blood, then looked at its head and saw on it neither grease nor blood; just as nothing of grease or blood stuck to it, so these have nothing of Islam stuck to them."
"4376","4370 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Hassan ibn Bilal, from Aishah, that she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him, she said: O Prophet of Allah, is there any one of us who does not hate death? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not hatred of death, but when death comes to the believer he is given glad tidings of Allah's pleasure and His Paradise, so nothing is more beloved to him than what has befallen him, so he loves meeting Allah and Allah loves meeting him; and when death comes to the disbeliever he is given tidings of Allah's punishment and wrath, so nothing is more hateful to him than what has come to him, so he hates meeting Allah and Allah hates meeting him."
"4377","4371 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Missisi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub, from Samurah ibn Jundub, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Attend Friday prayer and draw near the imam, for I know that some people will be delayed from entering Paradise because of their delaying from Friday, even if they are among its people. No one narrated these hadiths from Qatadah except Said ibn Bashir; Muhammad ibn Bakkar is alone in transmitting them."
"4378","4372 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Hammam, the brother of Abd al-Razzaq, narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them saying: Until when will you refrain from mentioning the wicked sinner? Expose him so that people may beware of him. No one narrated this hadith from Mamar except Abd al-Wahhab ibn Hammam; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari is alone in transmitting it."
"4379","4373 - Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: Abu Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adorn your festivals with takbir. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari is alone in transmitting it."
"4380","4374 - Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, saying: Ata ibn Muslim al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, he said: I was with al-Mughirah ibn Shubah when Ali was mentioned in his presence, so Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, Umar is in Paradise, Uthman is in Paradise, Ali is in Paradise, Talhah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf is in Paradise, Sad is in Paradise, and if I wished I could name the ninth. They said to him: Who is this? Said said: He himself, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the tenth. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah except al-Hasan ibn Salih, and no one narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Salih except Ata ibn Muslim; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari is alone in transmitting it."
"4381","4375 - Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Abdullah, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On honey there is a tenth; on every twelve waterskins, and there is nothing due on less than that. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"4382","4376 - Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Alhani narrated to me, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating cats and eating their price. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ziyad except Baqiyyah; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari is alone in transmitting it."
"4383","4377 - Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, he said: Rushdyn ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zuhrah ibn Mabad, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: How are you this morning, O so-and-so? He said: I praise Allah to you, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is what I wanted from you. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari is alone in transmitting it."
"4384","4378 - Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when the Negus died: Your brother Ashamah has died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and prayed over him as one prays over the dead, and said takbir over him four times. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, while people narrated it from Qatadah, from Ata, from Jabir."
"4385","4379 - Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir, he said: Banu Salimah wanted to move so as to be near the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O Banu Salimah, stay in your homes, for your footsteps will be recorded. No one narrated this hadith from Kahmas except Mutamir; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari is alone in transmitting it."
"4386","4380 - Abdullah ibn Wuhayb narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Subayh, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ghusl is with a sa and wudu is with a mudd. No one narrated this hadith from al-Rabi ibn Subayh except al-Walid; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari is alone in transmitting it."
"4387","4381 - Abdullah ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Abdullah al-Basri narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man sits between the four parts of a woman, ghusl becomes obligatory. No one narrated this hadith from Salim al-Khayyat except al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"4388","4382 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Salm al-Firyabi al-Maqdisi narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Ali and Abd al-Samad ibn Ali narrated to us, from their father Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hang the whip where the people of the house can see it, for it is discipline for them. No one narrated this hadith from Isa and Abd al-Samad except Sallam ibn Sulayman, while the well-known version is from the hadith of Dawud ibn Ali."
"4389","4383 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Salm al-Firyabi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Wazir al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn al-Safar narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Yunus al-Kinani narrated to me, from al-Amash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will resurrect two servants of His to whom He gave abundant wealth and children, and He will say to one of them: O so-and-so son of so-and-so. He will say: Here I am, my Lord, at Your service. He will say: Did I not give you abundant wealth and children? He will say: Yes indeed, my Lord. He will say: How did you act with what I gave you? He will say: I left it for my children fearing poverty for them. He will say: If you knew true knowledge you would have laughed little and wept much; what you feared for them has indeed befallen them. And He will say to the other: O so-and-so son of so-and-so, and he will say: Here I am, my Lord, at Your service. He will say to him: Did I not give you abundant wealth and children? He will say: Yes indeed, my Lord. He will say: How did you act with what I gave you? He will say: I spent in Your obedience, and I entrusted my children after me to Your good favor. He will say: If you knew true knowledge you would have laughed much and wept little; what you entrusted them to has indeed befallen them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Yusuf ibn al-Safar, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"4390","4384 - Abdullah ibn al-Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Mazyad al-Bayruti narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, he said: Hammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khawlani narrated to me, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to me, he said: Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one should preach to the people except a ruler, or one commanded, or a show-off. This hadith is not narrated from Hisham ibn Urwah except with this chain; al-Abbas ibn al-Walid is alone in transmitting it."
"4391","4385 - Abdullah ibn al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur informed me, he said: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss me then go out to prayer without performing wudu. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Said ibn Bashir, and no one narrated it from al-Zuhri except Mansur."
"4392","4386 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Abu Israil al-Mulai, whose name is Ismail, narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Juhayfah, he said: A delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing striped woolen garments, with traces of hardship upon them, and what he saw of their state grieved him, so he entered his house then came out and commanded charity and urged it, then said: Let a man give charity from a sa of his wheat, and let him give charity from a sa of his dates. A man came with a bundle and placed it, then people followed one after another until a pile of clothes and food gathered. The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brightened until it became as if gilded, then he said: Whoever establishes a good practice and it is acted upon after him, he will have its reward and the reward of whoever acts upon it, without anything diminishing from their rewards; and whoever establishes an evil practice and it is acted upon after him, upon him will be its sin and the sin of whoever acts upon it, without anything diminishing from their sins. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Abu Israil, and it is not narrated from Abu Juhayfah except with this chain."
"4393","4387 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Abu Israil al-Mulai narrated to us, from al-Fudayl ibn Amr, from Abu al-Hajjaj meaning Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha prayer until those praying had prayed, those waking had woken, and those praying tahajjud had prayed tahajjud, then he came out and said: Were it not that I would burden my ummah, I would command them to pray at this time, or this prayer, or something like this. No one narrated this hadith from al-Fudayl ibn Amr except Abu Israil; Ghassan ibn al-Rabi is alone in transmitting it."
"4394","4388 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Abu Israil al-Mulai narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may speak words intending nothing but to make people laugh, and he falls with them farther than the sky. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Said except with this chain; Ghassan is alone in transmitting it."
"4395","4389 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hurr, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, that he heard him say: Alqamah took my hand, Ibn Masud took Alqamah's hand, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took Ibn Masud's hand in the tashahhud in prayer: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Ibn Masud said: When you finish this you have finished your prayer; if you wish remain, and if you wish leave. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except Ghassan ibn al-Rabi."
"4396","4390 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Allah Almighty says: When My servant intends an evil deed and does not do it, do not record it; if he does it, record it as one; if he leaves it for My sake, record it as a good deed; and when he intends a good deed and does not do it, record it as a good deed, and if he does it, record it as ten like it up to seven hundredfold. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except Ghassan ibn al-Rabi."
"4397","4391 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Mutayr narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come upon a believer; Allah will send a pleasant wind before the Hour, and it will blow, and no believer will remain except that he dies. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"4398","4392 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Mutayr narrated to us, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about forgetfulness in prayer. He said: When you pray and see that you have completed your prayer while in doubt, then recite the tashahhud and leave, then prostrate two prostrations while sitting, then recite the tashahhud between them, and leave. This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain, from the hadith of Musa ibn Mutayr."
"4399","4393 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Maysarah al-Ashjai narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the procrastinating women. It was said: O Prophet of Allah, who are the procrastinating women? He said: The one whom her husband calls to his bed, and she says: Later, until sleep overcomes him. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"4400","4394 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once passed by graves with a moist palm stalk, split it into two, placed one on a grave and the other on another grave, then went on. We said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you do that? He said: As for one of them, he was being punished for talebearing, and as for the other, he would not guard against urine; and they will not be punished as long as these remain moist. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"4401","4395 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Maysarah al-Ashjai narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that he performed Hajj with him until he stood at Arafat, then he said to him: O Maysarah, climb the mountain. He said: So I did. When the people poured forth I went to urge my she-camel, and he said: Gently, a trot between two trots. When I crossed the mountain I said: Shall I dismount, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: Go on, O Maysarah. When we reached Muzdalifah he stood and called the adhan, then called the iqamah and prayed Maghrib, then called the iqamah and prayed the last Isha prayer. Then in the morning we did at al-Mashar as was done at the first Mashar, then he said: The polytheists would not pour forth from Arafat until the sun donned the mountains, becoming on their tops like the turbans of men on their faces, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pour forth until the sun set; and the polytheists would not pour forth from Muzdalifah until they said: Let Thabir shine, and they would not pour forth until the sun was on the mountain tops like the turbans of men on their faces, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pour forth before the sun rose. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain; Ghassan ibn al-Rabi is alone in transmitting it."
"4402","4396 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Umar and Abu Hurayrah, they said: Whoever walks to fulfill the need of his Muslim brother, Allah Almighty shades him with seventy-five thousand angels supplicating for him, and he keeps wading in mercy until he finishes; when he finishes Allah records for him a Hajj and an Umrah. And whoever visits a sick person, Allah shades him with seventy-five thousand angels; he does not lift a foot except a good deed is recorded for him, and he does not place a foot except a sin is removed from him and he is raised a degree thereby, until he sits in his place; when he sits, mercy covers him, and he remains so returning until he reaches his home. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"4403","4397 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath Abu al-Darda al-Antartusi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jami al-Muharibi, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the servant washes his hands the sins of his hands leave, and when he washes his face, rinses his mouth, brushes his teeth, inhales water and blows it out, and wipes his head, the sins of his hearing, sight and tongue leave, and when he washes his arms and feet he becomes as on the day his mother bore him; and whoever sleeps in a state of purity upon the remembrance of Allah does not ask Allah for anything until his soul is returned to him, of the matters of his world and Hereafter, except He gives it to him."
"4404","4398 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath Abu al-Darda narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Yala ibn Ata, from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad, from his father, he said: I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Farewell Hajj, and I prayed with him the dawn prayer at Mina. When he finished his prayer, there were two men behind the people who had not prayed with the people. He said: Bring me the two men. They were brought with their limbs trembling. He said: Did you not pray with us? They said: No, O Messenger of Allah, we had prayed in our tents and thought we would not catch the prayer. He said: Do not do so; when you have prayed in your tents then catch the prayer, pray it and it will be voluntary for you. One of them said: Seek forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: O Allah, forgive him. People crowded around the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I was that day among the strongest and most youthful of men, so I pushed through until I took the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed it on my chest, and I never felt anything cooler or more fragrant than the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4405","4399 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath Abu al-Darda narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Abu Ishaq al-Sabii, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while commanding ghusl on Friday from this minbar."
"4406","4400 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while commanding ghusl on Friday."
"4407","4401 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from a freed slave of Abu Qatadah, from Abu Qatadah, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no deed more beloved to Allah than a deed in these days, meaning: the ten, except a man who goes out striving with his wealth and soul and then does not return. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Qatadah except with this chain; Ibn Dhi Himayah is alone in transmitting it."
"4408","4402 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Ibn Amir, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the muadhdhin calls, Satan turns his back with flatulence; when he falls silent he comes forward until he intervenes between a man and his heart, reminding him of what he did not remember, until he confuses him in his prayer so he does not know how much he prayed. If one of you meets that and does not know how much he prayed, whether he added or omitted, let him prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness after giving the salam, for they are the two humiliators of Satan."
"4409","4403 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Shubah al-Azdi, from Qatadah ibn Diamah, from Abu Ayyub al-Azdi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Pray the first prayer before the time of Asr enters, Asr before the sun yellows, Maghrib before the twilight disappears, the last Isha at midnight, and Fajr before the sun rises."
"4410","4404 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sad ibn Hisham, he said: I asked Aishah about the night prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: His ablution water and tooth-stick would be placed for him, then Allah would send him whenever He willed to send him in the night, and he would use the tooth-stick and perform ablution, then stand and bow nine rakahs, and two rakahs while sitting; and when he was ill or did not rise at night, he would pray twelve rakahs."
"4411","4405 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer one day, and a man came with effort until breathlessness seized him, until he entered the row, and said: Praise belongs to Allah, much, good and blessed therein. When he finished he said: Which of you said the words? The man said: I did. He said: Twelve angels hastened to them, which of them would raise them."
"4412","4406 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you come to prayer, come with tranquility and dignity upon you; pray what you catch, and complete what you missed."
"4413","4407 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw sputum on the qiblah wall and became angry."
"4414","4408 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha prayer one night until midnight, then came out and prayed with us; when he finished he stood and addressed us, saying: People have prayed and slept, while you remain in prayer as long as you await the prayer."
"4415","4409 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and ordered an announcement: Prayer in congregation. Then he found two men quarreling, so he stood and addressed the people, saying: O people, I came out to inform you of Laylat al-Qadr, but I met so-and-so and so-and-so quarreling, and I forgot it; so seek it in the remaining ten, and seek it on the ninth, the seventh and the fifth."
"4416","4410 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to me, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Muhammad ibn Qays, that Umm Hani came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in Makkah for one of her needs, and found him praying Duha six rakahs."
"4417","4411 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Muhammad ibn Qays, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I was cut off with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he carried me on a camel; he passed by me while I was beating it at the rear of the people, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck it with a whip, and it kept among the foremost of the people. When we arrived at Makkah I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to return it to him, and found him praying the Duha prayer six rakahs."
"4418","4412 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn al-Saib, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about four rakahs before the Zuhr prayer, with no separation between them by taslim, when the sun declines? He said: It is an hour in which the gates of heaven are opened, and I love that a righteous deed of mine ascend therein."
"4419","4413 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, from al-Dahhak ibn Humrah, from Abu Nusayrah, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, from Atiq Abu Bakr, and from Imran ibn Husayn al-Khuzai, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, his sins and mistakes are expiated; when he sets out walking, twenty good deeds are recorded for him for every step; and when he finishes the prayer he is rewarded with the deeds of two hundred years."
"4420","4414 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Ata ibn Ajlan, from Mughirah ibn Hakim al-Sanani, referring it to Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever washes and performs ghusl on Friday, then goes early and arrives early, draws near where he hears the imam's sermon, then listens attentively, will have for every step the deeds of a year, its fasting and its standing."
"4421","4415 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Malih narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Dhi Himayah narrated to me, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki, from Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari, he said: We encamped with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Usfan, and the polytheists wanted to attack us while we were in the Zuhr prayer, saying: But there is a prayer dearer to them than their children, themselves and families, so attack them. Jibril came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. When the prayer was called, the Messenger of Allah ordered the people to wear arms and form two rows. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbir and they all said takbir, then he bowed and they all bowed, then he prostrated and the first row prostrated with him while the other stood guard. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose, the first row rose with him, and those in the other row fell in prostration. When they finished the two prostrations and stood, the first row moved back and the other row moved forward. When the polytheists saw what they did, they knew the news had reached them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbir and they all said takbir, then he bowed and they all bowed, then he prostrated and the first row prostrated while the other remained standing, until they finished two prostrations, then the other row fell in prostration, then they all sat and recited the tashahhud, then left. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Layla except Ibn Dhi Himayah."
"4422","4416 - Abdullah ibn al-Abbas al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn al-Shair narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will be rulers over you who delay the prayer, so pray the prayer at its time, and make your prayer with them voluntary. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Sufyan, and no one narrated it from Sufyan except Abu Ahmad; Hajjaj ibn al-Shair is alone in transmitting it."
"4423","4417 - Abdullah ibn al-Abbas al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said ibn Masruq, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have five names: I am Muhammad, Ahmad, al-Muqaffi, al-Hashir, the Prophet of repentance and the Prophet of battle. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Said except Ibrahim ibn Tahman; Ahmad ibn Hafs is alone in transmitting it."
"4424","4418 - Abdullah ibn al-Abbas al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Abi Zumayl narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The thief does not steal while stealing as a believer, nor does he drink wine while drinking it as a believer, nor does the adulterer commit adultery as a believer, but the doors of repentance are open. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah except Ubaydullah ibn Amr."
"4425","4419 - Abdullah ibn al-Abbas al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Sakuni narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah said: We find in ourselves what we dislike speaking about, though we would rather have all upon which the sun rises. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you indeed found that? They said: Yes. He said: That is pure faith."
"4426","4420 - Abdullah ibn al-Abbas al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Sakuni narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most complete of the believers in faith are the best of them in character, and the best of you are the best of you to their families. No one narrated these two hadiths from Husayn except Abbad ibn al-Awwam; Abd al-Rahim ibn Muhammad al-Sakuni is alone in transmitting them."
"4427","4421 - Abdullah ibn al-Abbas al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been permitted to speak about an angel of Allah among the bearers of the Throne: between his earlobe and his shoulder is a journey of seventy years. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Musa ibn Uqbah, nor from Musa except Ibrahim ibn Tahman; Ahmad ibn Hafs is alone in transmitting it."
"4428","4422 - Abdullah ibn Sulayman ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Abi Abbad al-Qalzumi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most complete of the believers in faith are the best of them in character, the humble and gentle, who love others and are loved; and he is not of us who neither loves nor is loved. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Uyaynah except Yaqub ibn Abi Abbad."
"4429","4423 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf the judge narrated to us, from Abu Ayyub al-Ifriqi, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Umar, from Umar and Sad, they said: We saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the two khuffs. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ayyub al-Ifriqi except Abu Yusuf the judge; Abu al-Rabi is alone in transmitting it."
"4430","4424 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Israil narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salamah al-Aftas narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to Quba riding and walking. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Yahya ibn Said, nor from Yahya except Abdullah ibn Salamah; al-Hasan ibn Israil is alone in transmitting it."
"4431","4425 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Balkhi narrated to us, he said: Junadah ibn Salm narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw in a dream a black woman with disheveled hair who went out until she stood at Mahyaah, which is al-Juhfah, so I interpreted that the epidemic of Madinah was transferred to al-Juhfah."
"4432","4426 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn al-Sabbah al-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Sad, from al-Hasan, from Utayy ibn Damrah, from Ubayy ibn Kab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The angels washed Adam and said takbir over him four times, and said: This is your practice, O children of Adam."
"4433","4427 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: My father Ali ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: My father Rashid ibn Abdullah informed me, from Nafi, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me a hadith and make it brief. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Pray the prayer of one bidding farewell, for if you do not see Him, He sees you; despair of what is in people's hands and you will be rich; and beware of what requires an apology."
"4434","4428 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Amir al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj. No one narrated this hadith from Bakr except Amir; Abd al-Warith is alone in transmitting it."
"4435","4429 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Habib ibn Muhammad al-Jarudi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from his father, from Sahl ibn Sad, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man should not sit between a man and his son in a gathering."
"4436","4430 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Musa ibn Atiyyah al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best to which mounts are ridden are this mosque of mine and the Ancient House."
"4437","4431 - Abdullah ibn Najiyah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abis narrated to us, from Badr ibn al-Khalil, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, Abu al-Jahhaf and Kathir al-Nawwa, all of whom heard Atiyyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: O Ali, these two are the masters of the elderly people of Paradise among the first and the last, meaning: Abu Bakr and Umar; do not inform them of that, O Ali. No one narrated this hadith from Badr ibn al-Khalil and those with him except Ali ibn Abis; al-Jubayri is alone in transmitting it."
"4438","4432 - Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Qazaah narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: An accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise, and one Umrah to the next is expiation for what is between them. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Umayyah except Humayd ibn al-Aswad; al-Hasan ibn Qazaah is alone in transmitting it."
"4439","4433 - Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nashai narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Yahya al-Taymi narrated to us, from Misar ibn Kidam, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man does not leave faith except by denying what he entered into. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Ismail ibn Yahya al-Taymi; Muhammad ibn Harb is alone in transmitting it."
"4440","4434 - Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Sufyan al-Mustamli narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Sulayman al-Qari Abu Sulayman al-Karizi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar said: I recited Surah al-Waqiah to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when I reached: refreshment and fragrance, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: refreshment and fragrance, O Ibn Umar. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Hammad ibn Salamah, and no one narrated it from Hammad except Dawud ibn Sulayman al-Karizi; Harun ibn Sufyan is alone in transmitting it."
"4441","4435 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Najiyah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Abu Hurrah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The boy is pledged for his aqeeqah; it is slaughtered for him on his seventh day. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hurrah except Isa ibn Shuayb."
"4442","4436 - Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Wasil narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Ata al-Basri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbir over his son Ibrahim four takbirs. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Salih except Musab ibn al-Miqdam, and Ata al-Basri is Ata ibn Ajlan."
"4443","4437 - Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's greeting with one finger, pointing with it, is the act of the Jews. No one narrated this hadith from Thawr except Abu Khalid al-Ahmar; Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"4444","4438 - Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Yahya al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan al-Rahawi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah and Abdullah ibn Ali narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever goes out with a funeral until it is buried will have two qirats of reward. It was said: What is a qirat? He said: Like Uhud."
"4445","4439 - Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Yahya al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah and Abdullah ibn Ali narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs wudu well, his sins leave his hearing, sight, hands and feet. Abu Zabyah al-Himsi, while with Abu Umamah, said: And I heard Amr ibn Abasah narrate that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: There is no servant who sleeps in purity then remembers Allah, then wakes in the night and supplicates to Allah, except Allah gives him what he asks of the matters of this world and the Hereafter."
"4446","4440 - Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Yahya al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah and Abdullah ibn Ali narrated to me, from Adi ibn Thabit and Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who performs wudu and washes his hands except his sins leave his hands, then washes his face except his sins leave his face, then washes his arms except his sins leave his arms, then wipes his head except his sins leave his head, then washes his feet except his sins leave his feet. No one narrated these hadiths from Abdullah ibn Ali - who is Abu Ayyub al-Ifriqi - except Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Sinan; Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Sinan is alone in transmitting them."
"4447","4441 - Abdullah ibn Zaydan ibn Yazid al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Hayyaji narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Arhabi informed us, he said: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whom Allah hates: a lying king, a poor man who is arrogant, and a rich miser. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid except Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad; Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"4448","4442 - Abdullah ibn Zaydan al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Hamzah ibn Awn al-Masudi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Miskin narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Abu Ayyub, he said: I never prayed behind your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except I heard him when he finished saying: O Allah, forgive me all my faults and sins; O Allah, revive me, mend me, and guide me to righteous deeds and morals, for none guides to their righteousness nor turns their evil from me except You. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Ayyub except with this chain; Muhammad ibn al-Salt is alone in transmitting it."
"4449","4443 - Abdullah ibn Zaydan al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Tarif al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ruasi narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, he said: Said ibn Amr al-Qurashi narrated to me, from Umm Kabshah, a woman of Banu Udhrah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, permit me to go out with such-and-such army. He said: No. She said: O Prophet of Allah, I do not want fighting; I only want to treat the wounded and sick. He said: Were it not that it would become a precedent, it being said: So-and-so woman went out, I would have permitted you. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Kabshah except with this chain; al-Hasan ibn Salih is alone in transmitting it."
"4450","4444 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Numan al-Qazzaz al-Basri narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Yazid al-Sudai narrated to us, he said: My father Ali ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you fled from his provision it would catch him just as death catches him. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Marzuq except Ali ibn Yazid, and it is not narrated from Abu Said except with this chain."
"4451","4445 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Numan al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, from Matar al-Warraq, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The angels curse one of you when he points at his brother with a piece of iron, even if he is his full brother. No one narrated this hadith from Matar except al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, nor from al-Mughirah except Ishaq; Abu Hisham is alone in transmitting it."
"4452","4446 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Numan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Ala al-Hamdani narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Abdullah ibn Sulayman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Bashir ibn Sallam narrated to me, from his father, he said: I entered with Muhammad ibn Ali and another man of the Alawis upon Jabir ibn Abdullah, and he said: Who are you two? The two Alawis gave him their lineage and he recognized them, and I gave him my lineage and he said: I do not know you. I said: If you do not know me, Allah knows me. He said: What use is Jabir's knowledge to you? I said: Pray with us as you saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr when the shadow was like a sandal strap, Asr when the shadow was like it plus a sandal strap, Maghrib when the sun set, Isha when the twilight disappeared, and Fajr when dawn broke. Then the next day he prayed Zuhr when the shadow of everything was like it, then prayed Asr when the shadow of everything was twice it, then prayed Maghrib when the sun set, then prayed Isha with the last third of the night."
"4453","4447 - Abdullah ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Numan al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is best? He said: One whose blood is shed and whose horse is hamstrung. Thus Sufyan ibn Waki narrated this hadith from Ibn Numayr, from al-Amash, while people narrated it from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir."
"4454","4448 - Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Muhammad ibn Shurahbil informed me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah lifted a curtain and opened a door during his illness, looked at the people praying behind Abu Bakr, was pleased with that and said: Praise belongs to Allah; no prophet has died until a man of his ummah leads him in prayer. Then he turned to the people and said: O people, whoever of you is afflicted with a calamity after me, let him take consolation in his calamity through me for the calamity that befalls him, for no one of my ummah after me will be afflicted with the like of his calamity through me. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman except Musab ibn Muhammad ibn Shurahbil; Abdullah ibn Jafar is alone in transmitting it."
"4455","4449 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhtan al-Shirazi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Muhammad al-Ziyadabadi al-Shirazi narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Qays ibn Sad, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Upon every joint or upon every limb of the children of Adam each day is charity, and two rakahs of Duha suffice for all of that. No one narrated this hadith from Qays ibn Sad except Hisham ibn Hassan, nor from Hisham except Salim ibn Nuh; Ali ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"4456","4450 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yaqub al-Khazzaz al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Shabbah al-Numayri narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan ibn Atiyyah al-Awfi narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed would spread his left and erect his right. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan; Umar ibn Shabbah is alone in transmitting it."
"4457","4451 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Tuwayt al-Ramli al-Bazzaz narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali, the nephew of Rawwad, narrated to us, he said: Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, in one chain, and he said: Rawwad narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Travel is a portion of torment; it deprives one of you of his sleep, food, drink and pleasure, so when one of you finishes his need let him hasten back to his family. No one narrated this hadith from Malik, from Rabiah, except Rawwad, while the well-known version is from Malik, from Sumayy."
"4458","4452 - Abdullah ibn Musa ibn Abi Uthman al-Anmati narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: May the fasting person kiss? He said: What harm is there in that? It is a sweet basil he smells. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman al-Taymi except Mutamir; Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Aruzzi is alone in transmitting it."
"4459","4453 - Abdullah ibn Musa ibn Abi Uthman al-Anmati narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Sari ibn Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be cupped when seventeen days of the month had passed, and nineteen, and twenty-one. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sari ibn Yahya except Maslamah ibn Ali; al-Hakam ibn Musa is alone in transmitting it, and no one narrated it from Muhammad ibn Sirin except al-Sari ibn Yahya."
"4460","4454 - Abdullah ibn al-Saqr al-Sukkari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi, he said: I heard Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman and Yahya ibn Said narrating, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, she said: Prayer was two rakahs by two rakahs when first made obligatory, then the prayer of residence was increased, while the travel prayer was left upon the first obligation. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya and Rabiah except Usamah ibn Zayd; Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi is alone in transmitting it."
"4461","4455 - Abdullah ibn al-Saqr al-Sukkari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Magians of this ummah are those who deny Allah's decrees; if they fall ill do not visit them, if you meet them do not greet them, and if they die do not attend them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Baqiyyah; Muhammad ibn Musaffa is alone in transmitting it."
"4462","4456 - Abdullah ibn al-Saqr al-Sukkari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muttalib ibn al-Saib ibn Abi Wadaah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Musa ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah al-Makhzumi narrated to me, he said: My uncle Musab ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Umm Salamah bint Abi Umayyah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), people would pray with the one praying not letting his sight go beyond the place of his feet. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"4463","4457 - Abdullah ibn al-Saqr al-Sukkari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bashir ibn Khallad narrated to us, he said: Amat al-Wahid bint Yamin ibn Abdullah al-Nasri narrated to me, she said: I entered upon Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi and heard him say: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Place the imam in the middle and close the gaps so Satan does not slip through them, and place your sandals between your feet. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; Yahya ibn Bashir is alone in transmitting it."
"4464","4458 - Abdullah ibn al-Saqr al-Sukkari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir, he said: I said to al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra: Describe the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to me. She said: Had you seen him, you would have seen the sun rising. This hadith is not narrated from al-Rubayyi except with this chain; Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi is alone in transmitting it."
"4465","4459 - Abdullah ibn al-Saqr al-Sukkari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Bakkar ibn Muhammad ibn Jaristat narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Umm Khalid bint Khalid narrated to me, she said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and looked at the seal of prophethood between his shoulders. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Bakkar ibn Muhammad; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"4466","4460 - Abdullah ibn Shuayb Abu al-Qasim al-Harbi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ward ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Uthman al-Batti, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that a slave owned jointly by ten was freed by nine of them, while the tenth refused to free him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, what of my shares? He said: Your shares remain in him. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Uthman al-Batti, nor from Uthman except Adi ibn al-Fadl; Ward ibn Abdullah is alone in transmitting it."
"4467","4461 - Abdullah ibn Shuayb Abu al-Qasim al-Harbi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Makhlad ibn Janah, the freed slave of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to us, he said: Abu Yusuf the judge narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ali, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, circumambulated the House, prayed two rakahs behind the Station of Ibrahim, and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah; in the Messenger of Allah there is a good example for you. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Ali - who is Abu Ayyub al-Ifriqi - except Abu Yusuf the judge."
"4468","4462 - Abdullah ibn Quraysh al-Asadi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: I found in the hearing of al-Faraj ibn al-Yaman al-Kardali, he said: Sayf ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent my maternal uncle to a man of Yemen who had married his father's wife, saying: If you find him, strike his neck and take charge of his wealth. No one narrated this hadith from Hamzah al-Zayyat except Sayf ibn Muhammad."
"4469","4463 - Abdullah ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Saqri al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn al-Akhyal narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered on the day of the conquest of Makkah wearing a black turban. No one narrated this hadith from al-Thawri except Muawiyah ibn Hisham; Ishaq ibn al-Akhyal is alone in transmitting it."
"4470","4464 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ali, the nephew of Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, he said: Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah and al-Musayyab ibn Sharik narrated to us, saying: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Kab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about: Their mark is on their faces from the trace of prostration: It is light on the Day of Resurrection. No one raised this hadith from Abu Jafar al-Razi except Rawwad and al-Musayyab; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari is alone in transmitting it."
"4471","4465 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Dabbi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ishaq ibn Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas narrated to us, he said: Umar Abu Hafs al-Abdi narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution, running his fingers through his beard from beneath his chin, saying: With this my Lord Almighty commanded me. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Umar Abu Hafs al-Abdi."
"4472","4466 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Maymun ibn Najih Abu al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I desire jihad but I cannot undertake it? He said: Is any of your parents still alive? He said: My mother. He said: Then present your excuse to Allah through devotion to her; if you do that you are a pilgrim, a performer of Umrah and a warrior, when your mother is pleased; so fear Allah and honor her. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Maymun ibn Najih; Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"4473","4467 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib narrated to us, from Musab ibn Hayyan, from his brother Muqatil ibn Hayyan, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not rise from a gathering until he said: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. Then he would say: It is expiation for what occurs in the gathering. Thus Muqatil narrated it from Abu al-Aliyah, from Rafi ibn Khadij, and no one narrated it from Muqatil except his brother Musab ibn Hayyan; Yunus ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it. Al-Hajjaj ibn Dinar narrated it from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Abu Barzah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4474","4468 - Abdullah ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Madaini narrated to us, he said: Abu Mamar Salih ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Abi Khubzah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade squatting in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Sallam ibn Abi Khubzah; Salih ibn Harb is alone in transmitting it."
"4475","4469 - Abdullah ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Madaini narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Bazi al-Khassaf al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Abu Janab, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Ibn Masud, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade fasting three days: hastening a day before sighting, and the day of Adha, and Fitr. No one narrated this hadith from Talhah ibn Musarrif except Abu Janab, nor from Abu Janab except Said ibn Maslamah; Ahmad ibn Bazi is alone in transmitting it."
"4476","4470 - Abdullah ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Madaini narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal al-Anmati narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: Abu Maryam Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Harun ibn Sad, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while the sun was rising: Do you know where this ascends, O Abu Dharr? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: It ascends and sets, then runs to its resting place, comes to the Throne and falls prostrate, until it is told: Rise from your rising place; though it had been told: Return from where you came, so it rises from its west, and that is when: no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good through its faith - the verse. No one narrated this hadith from Harun ibn Said except Abu Maryam; al-Hakam ibn Marwan is alone in transmitting it."
"4477","4471 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah al-Qumasi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from al-Shabi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty and faith are joined; they do not separate except together. No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Mighwal except Abu Ishaq al-Fazari; Muhammad ibn Ubaydah is alone in transmitting it."
"4478","4472 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah al-Qumasi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Harasah narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Zayyat, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from his father, from Ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever commits a sin then knows that Allah has seen it is forgiven, even if he does not seek forgiveness. No one narrated this hadith from Hamzah al-Zayyat except Ibrahim ibn Harasah; Muhammad ibn Ubaydah is alone in transmitting it."
"4479","4473 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Rajjani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: We entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a Friday, with food before him from which he was eating, and he said: Come near and eat of this food. I, or one of us, said: We are fasting, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Did you fast yesterday? We said: No. He said: Do you intend to fast tomorrow? We said: No. He said: Then come near and eat of this food, for Friday is not fasted alone; it is taken as a festival. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah except Said al-Maqburi, nor from Said except Abdullah ibn Said; Safwan ibn Isa is alone in transmitting it."
"4480","4474 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said al-Simmari al-Naqid narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Shaylamani narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Ismail al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I gave glad tidings to Bilal, and he said to me: O Abdullah, with what do you give me glad tidings? I said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Bilal will come on the Day of Resurrection upon a mount of gold with reins of pearls and rubies, with a banner followed by the muadhdhins, and he will admit them to Paradise, so much so that he will admit whoever called the adhan forty mornings seeking thereby the Face of Allah Almighty."
"4481","4475 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said al-Simmari narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Shaylamani narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Salih, the freed slave of al-Tawamah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any youth who marries in his youth, his devil cries out: Woe to him, woe to him; he has protected his religion from me."
"4482","4476 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said al-Simmari narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Shaylamani narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Ismail al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Salih, the freed slave of al-Tawamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Were only one day left of my life, I would meet Allah Almighty with a wife, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The worst of you are your unmarried ones. No one narrated these hadiths from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Khalid ibn Ismail; al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan is alone in transmitting them."
"4483","4477 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Khallad al-Qattan al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Yahya, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: Muadh ibn Jabal used to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then come to his people and lead them in the prayer he had prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Yahya except Said ibn Abi Arubah; Abd al-Ala is alone in transmitting it."
"4484","4478 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Khallad al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasna narrated to us, from Abu al-Aliyah al-Barra, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, that when al-Hajjaj entered upon her, it was said to her: This is the commander al-Hajjaj. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among Thaqif there is a liar and a destroyer; as for the liar we have seen him, and as for the destroyer, you are he. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Aliyah except al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasna."
"4485","4479 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Khallad al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, he said: al-Saq ibn Hazn narrated to us, from Uqayl al-Jadi, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: O Ibn Masud, which bonds of faith are firmest? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The firmest bonds of Islam are allegiance for Allah, love for Him, and hatred for Him. Then he said: O Ibn Masud. I said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah, saying it three times. He said: Do you know which people are best? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The best of people are the best of them in deeds, when they understand their religion. Then he said: O Ibn Masud. I said: Here I am, O Messenger of Allah, three times. He said: Do you know which people are most knowledgeable? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The most knowledgeable of people are the most discerning of truth when people differ, even if deficient in deeds, even if crawling on his buttocks. Those before me differed into seventy-two sects; three of them were saved and the rest perished: a group that supported the kings and fought them over their religion and the religion of Isa son of Maryam, so they seized them, killed them and cut them with saws; and a group that had no strength to confront the kings nor to live among them calling them to the religion of Allah and the religion of Isa son of Maryam, so they wandered in the lands and became monks. He said: They are those about whom Allah said: And monasticism which they invented, We did not prescribe it for them - the verse. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in me, follows me and affirms me has observed it with its true observance, and whoever does not follow me, they are the doomed. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Uqayl al-Jadi; al-Saq ibn Hazn is alone in transmitting it."
"4486","4480 - Abdullah ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Uqayl, a man of Banu Jadah, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim al-Adawi, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah protect you from rulers who come after me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is that? He said: Whoever enters upon them, believes their lies and aids them in their wrongdoing is not of me and I am not of him, and he will never come to me at the Basin; and whoever does not enter upon them, does not believe their lies nor aids them in their wrongdoing, he is of me and I am of him, and he will come to my Basin. No flesh grown from unlawful earnings will enter Paradise; every flesh grown from unlawful earnings, the Fire is more deserving of it. People are two going forth: one selling himself and destroying it, and one ransoming himself and freeing it. Prayer is proof, fasting is a shield, and charity extinguishes sin as water extinguishes fire. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Uqayl al-Jadi; Ibrahim ibn Tahman is alone in transmitting it."
"4487","4481 - Abdullah ibn Ali al-Jarudi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Ismail al-Suddi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, this greeting to you we know how to greet you, but how do we pray upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious; O Allah, favor Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You favored Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. No one narrated this hadith from al-Suddi except Ibrahim ibn Tahman; Ahmad ibn Hafs is alone in transmitting it."
"4488","4482 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Rashid al-Sulami al-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Mihran ibn Hakim, the brother of Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, whom should I honor? He said: Your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your mother. I said: Then whom? He said: Then your father, then the nearest, then the nearest. Mihran ibn Hakim did not transmit any hadith other than this; Ibrahim ibn Tahman is alone in transmitting it."
"4489","4483 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn ibn Rashid al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said ibn Masruq, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prostrates, let him be balanced and not spread his forearms as a dog spreads them."
"4490","4484 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn ibn Rashid al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said ibn Masruq, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell from a horse of his in Madinah and his foot was dislocated, so we visited him while he was sitting in Aishah's chamber. We stood behind him and prayed. Then we came to him another time and found him sitting, glorifying Allah in the obligatory prayer, so we stood behind him, and he gestured with his hand: Sit. When he finished the prayer he said: When your imam prays standing, pray standing; and when he prays sitting, pray sitting; and do not stand while he sits, as the Persians do with their great ones."
"4491","4485 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said, from Sulayman, from Abu Wail, from Qays ibn Abi Gharazah, he said: We used to trade in Madinah and call ourselves brokers, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by us and named us with a name better than what we named ourselves, saying: O company of merchants, idle talk and oaths attend these sales, so mix them with charity."
"4492","4486 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said ibn Masruq, from Sulayman, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The purest of what a man eats is from his earnings, and his child is from his earnings."
"4493","4487 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said ibn Masruq, from Sulayman, he said: Umarah ibn Umayr informed me, from his paternal aunt, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like of that. No one narrated these hadiths from Umar ibn Said except Ibrahim ibn Tahman; Ahmad ibn Hafs is alone in transmitting them."
"4494","4488 - Abdullah ibn Umar al-Saffar al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a false oath by which he seizes the wealth of a Muslim man will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection while He is angry with him. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Abdullah ibn Bazi; Yahya ibn Ghaylan is alone in transmitting it."
"4495","4489 - Abdullah ibn Umar al-Saffar al-Tustari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bazi narrated to us, from Abu Hanifah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that a questioner asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Does only water necessitate water? He said: When the two circumcised parts meet and the head disappears, ghusl becomes obligatory, whether he ejaculates or not. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Shuayb except Abu Hanifah, nor from Abu Hanifah except Abdullah ibn Bazi; Yahya ibn Ghaylan is alone in transmitting it."
"4496","4490 - Abdullah ibn Umar as-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, from Abu Hanifah, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutilation. No one narrated this hadith from Alqamah ibn Marthad except Abu Hanifah, and no one narrated it from Abu Hanifah except Abdullah ibn Bazi'; Yahya ibn Ghaylan is alone in transmitting it."
"4497","4491 - Abdullah ibn Umar as-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, from Hisham al-Qirdusi, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian, and any woman who marries without a guardian, her marriage is invalid. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Abdullah ibn Bazi'; Yahya ibn Ghaylan is alone in transmitting it."
"4498","4492 - Abdullah ibn Umar as-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, from Abu Hanifah, he said: Atiyah narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a woman be married together with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt. No one narrated this hadith from Atiyah except Abu Hanifah, and no one narrated it from Abu Hanifah except Abdullah ibn Bazi'; Yahya ibn Ghaylan is alone in transmitting it."
"4499","4493 - Abdullah ibn Umar as-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, from Sulaym, the freedman of ash-Sha'bi, from ash-Sha'bi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not to be married together with her maternal aunt, nor a maternal aunt over her sister's daughter, nor a woman over her paternal aunt, nor a paternal aunt over her brother's daughter; the younger is not married over the elder, nor the elder over the younger. No one narrated this hadith from Sulaym, the freedman of ash-Sha'bi, except Abdullah ibn Bazi'; Yahya ibn Ghaylan is alone in transmitting it."
"4500","4494 - Abu Sharra'ah Abdullah ibn Sharra'ah al-Qaysi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: an-Namir ibn Kulthum an-Namari narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: Rabi'ah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his permission regarding the first departure, then Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him and said: O Muhammad, Allah sends greetings of peace upon you, and He says to Rabi'ah: Do not depart with the first departure, for nothing from a beloved is too little. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; an-Namir ibn Kulthum an-Namari is alone in transmitting it."
"4501","4495 - Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Khalid ar-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Labbayk on behalf of Shubrumah, so he said: Have you performed Hajj? He said: No. He said: Perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj for Shubrumah. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Hammad ibn Salamah, and no one narrated it from Hammad except Yazid ibn Harun; Abdur-Rahman ibn Khalid ar-Raqqi is alone in transmitting it."
"4502","4496 - Abdullah ibn Mandah ibn al-Walid al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ma'bad ibn Nubatah, from Nu'aym ibn Abdullah al-Mujmir, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ma'mar ibn Abdullah al-Adawi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one hoards except a sinner. No one narrated this hadith from Nu'aym al-Mujmir except Ma'bad ibn Nubatah, and no one narrated it from Ma'bad except Ibn Jurayj; Hajjaj ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"4503","4497 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: an-Nu'man ibn Abdus-Salam narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abdur-Rahman and at-Tustari and others narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Umm Atiyah, she said: A daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, so he said: Wash her three times or five times, or more than that if you see fit, with water and lote leaves, and put something of camphor in the last washing; when you finish, inform me. When we finished we informed him, so he threw his waist-wrapper to us and said: Wrap her in it as an inner garment. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Abdur-Rahman except an-Nu'man ibn Abdus-Salam and Abu Dawud."
"4504","4498 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Umarah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna ibn Abdullah ibn Anas narrated to me, from Thumamah ibn Abdullah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Qatadah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of my ummah are pardoned, except one who does a deed by night, then in the morning his Lord has concealed it, yet he says: O so-and-so, last night I did such-and-such; or he said: He spends the night while his Lord conceals him, then in the morning he exposes Allah's covering over him. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Qatadah except with this chain; al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani is alone in transmitting it."
"4505","4499 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Imran narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Ali Abu Hafs narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah narrated to me, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasna narrated to me, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, regarding His saying: (And during the night, pray Tahajjud as an extra for you), he said: The extra prayer was only for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasna except Abu Qutaybah and Ali ibn Nasr al-Jahdami."
"4506","4500 - Abdullah ibn Bundar al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Imran narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran narrated to us, from Jabir, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the snake and said: It and man were created alike; if it sees him it frightens him, and if it bites him it pains him, so kill it wherever you find it. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Imran al-Qattan, and no one narrated it from Imran except Abu Dawud; Abdullah ibn Imran is alone in transmitting it."
"4507","4501 - Abdullah ibn Bundar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Mansur, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: We used to eat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we could hear the food glorifying Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Isra'il."
"4508","4502 - Abdullah ibn Bundar narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Minqari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith at-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, he said: We were with Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz on the day of Fitr, and he brought out dates to us and said: Eat before you go out early. We said to him: Do you have anything on this matter? He said: Yes; Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to eat on the day of Fitr before going out early, and he commanded the people to do that. This hadith is not narrated from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz except with this chain; al-Waqidi is alone in transmitting it."
"4509","4503 - Abdullah ibn Bundar narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Minqari narrated to us, he said: as-Sakan Abu Amr al-Burjumi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a servant and he knows that it is from Allah, except that Allah records gratitude for it for him before he even praises Him for it; and no servant commits a sin and regrets it, except that Allah records His forgiveness for him before he even seeks forgiveness; and no servant buys a garment for a dinar or half a dinar and praises Allah when he wears it, except that before it reaches his knees Allah forgives him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad except al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham, and no one narrated it from al-Walid except as-Sakan al-Burjumi; Sulayman ibn Dawud is alone in transmitting it."
"4510","4504 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Usayd al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Maslamah ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mus'ab al-Qarqasani narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever relieves a distress of a believer, Allah Almighty will make for him on the Day of Resurrection two branches of light upon the Sirat, by whose light a world of people beyond count except by the Lord of Might will see. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Muhammad ibn Mus'ab; al-Ala ibn Maslamah is alone in transmitting it."
"4511","4505 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Usayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Subayh narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Ma'ni narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Aisha, she said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there were two cushions in the house with images on them, so he said: What are these, O Aisha? She said: I made them for you to recline upon. He said: Do you not know that the image-makers will be told on the Day of Resurrection: Give life to what you fashioned. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar, from Aisha, except with this chain; Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Ma'ni is alone in transmitting it, and Mansur is Ibn Zadahan."
"4512","4506 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Usayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Anas Kathir ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalid al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Sulaym al-Makki narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever Allah grants a handsome face and a handsome name, and places him in a position not disgraceful to him, is among Allah Almighty's elite of His creation. And Ibn Abbas said: The poet said... This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Kathir ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"4513","4507 - Abdullah ibn as-Sabbah al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Hashim ibn al-Walid al-Harawi narrated to us, he said: an-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded a caller on a rainy day to proclaim: Pray in your dwellings. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except an-Nadr ibn Shumayl."
"4514","4508 - Abdullah ibn as-Sabbah narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn as-Salt narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn ar-Rabi' narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Wa'il, from az-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you carry, then delay, for the leg is bound and the hand is suspended. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Bakr ibn Wa'il."
"4515","4509 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq at-Tustari ad-Daqiqi narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq Abu Yusuf al-Qalusi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ali al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Imran Abu al-Awwam narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: that Abu Bakr led the people in prayer, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and prayed behind him in the row, in a single garment wrapped around himself. No one narrated this hadith from Imran al-Qattan except Abu Ali al-Hanafi."
"4516","4510 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Usayd al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ishaq al-Kinani narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ata, that he narrated to him from Aisha, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, will they return with a Hajj and an Umrah while I return with only a Hajj? So he commanded her brother, and he went out with her and she performed Umrah. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid ibn Dinar except Yunus ibn Bukayr."
"4517","4511 - Abdullah ibn Imran ibn Musa al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Ali ibn Abdullah al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Hubayrah al-Mu'addib al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Sinan al-Ansari narrated to us, from Talhah ibn Amr, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the Day of Resurrection Allah will command a caller who will call out: I made a lineage and you made a lineage; I made the noblest of you the most God-fearing of you, but you refused except to say: So-and-so son of so-and-so is better than so-and-so son of so-and-so. So today I raise My lineage and lower yours: where are the God-fearing?"
"4518","Those named Abdan. 4512 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sahbal ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hadrad al-Aslami, he said: A Jew was owed four dirhams by me and he clung to me, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to go out to Khaybar. I asked him to wait until I return, saying: Perhaps we will gain some spoils. He brought me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give him his right - twice. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you intend to go out to Khaybar, and perhaps Allah will grant us spoils there. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give him his right. And when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said something three times, he was not to be argued with. He said: I had a waist-wrapper on me and a headband on my head; when I went out I said: Buy this waist-wrapper from me, so he bought it for the dirhams he was owed by me, and I wrapped myself with the headband that was on my head. Then a woman wearing a shawl passed by and dressed me with it. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hadrad except with this chain; Qutaybah is alone in transmitting it."
"4519","4513 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman ad-Duba'i narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Razin, from his brother, from Layth, from Ibn Sabit, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has forbidden the singing slave-girl, her sale, her price, teaching her, and listening to her. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Abi Razin except Ja'far ibn Sulayman."
"4520","4514 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: The emigrant women used to pray Fajr with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return wrapped in their woolen cloaks, unrecognized in the darkness. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Aswad except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"4521","4515 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Sayyar al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyib, from al-Fudayl ibn Amr, from Aisha bint Talhah, from Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, she said: A boy died in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was said: A sparrow from the sparrows of Paradise. Aisha said: Glad tidings for him, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Do you not know that Allah created Paradise and created Hell, and created people for this one and people for that one. No one narrated this hadith from al-Fudayl ibn Amr except al-Ala ibn al-Musayyib."
"4522","4516 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Usm, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: A man prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), bowing before he bowed and rising before he rose. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: Who did this? He said: I did, O Messenger of Allah; I wanted to know whether you notice that or not. He said: Beware of defective prayer; when the imam bows, bow, and when he rises, rise. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Usm except Ayyub ibn Jabir; Qutaybah is alone in transmitting it."
"4523","4517 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated to us, he said: Nafi', the freedman of Yusuf as-Sulami, narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: (Every time their skins ripen, We replace them with other skins) was recited before Umar, so Umar said: Repeat it. He repeated it, and Mu'adh ibn Jabal said: I have its explanation: they are replaced a hundred times in an hour. Umar said: This is how I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith is not narrated from Umar except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"4524","4518 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Muzahim ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, he said: My father Muzahim narrated to me, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Asid, from Muharrish al-Ka'bi, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered al-Ji'ranah, and the people of al-Ji'ranah learned of his entry and gathered around him in large numbers. He raised his hands, and it was as if I am looking at the whiteness of his armpits and sides, like the whiteness of stalks. He said: O people, away from me. They moved away from him until he came to the mosque, prayed as much as Allah willed, then mounted his riding camel, faced the valley of Sarif until he reached the road to Madinah in the morning, and by morning he was in Makkah as one who had spent the night there. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Muzahim except Qutaybah."
"4525","4519 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, from Umar ibn Amir, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Anas ibn Malik: that Abu Talhah called out for Hajj and Umrah together, while his knee was striking the knee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Dinar except Umar ibn Amir; Salim ibn Nuh is alone in transmitting it."
"4526","4520 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: ar-Rabi' ibn Badr narrated to us, from an-Nahhas ibn Qahm, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Immoral women who marry themselves off: no marriage is valid except with a guardian, two witnesses, and a dowry, little or much. No one narrated this hadith from an-Nahhas except ar-Rabi' ibn Badr."
"4527","4521 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Munkadir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, that he said: I was present with Ali ibn Abi Talib and al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib when they were disputing before Umar ibn al-Khattab over the inheritance of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The people said: Judge between them, O Commander of the Believers. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Allah Almighty says in His Book: (Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth glorifies Allah, and He is the Mighty, the Wise), and he recited until His saying: (And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it). Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to place it among the poor, the orphans, the wayfarer, the guests of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his horsemen, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away; then Abu Bakr administered it, then I administered it, placing it where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr placed it. Now it has occurred to me to entrust it to you, O Ali, so place it where you saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) place it, and where you saw me place it. This hadith is not narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except with this chain; his son is alone in transmitting it from him."
"4528","4522 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, he said: The nephew of az-Zuhri narrated to me, he said: az-Zuhri narrated to me, from Humayd ibn Abdur-Rahman, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Time will draw near, and knowledge will decrease. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jabir except Sadaqah ibn Khalid; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"4529","4523 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud al-Harrani narrated to us, from Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked the lamp when morning came. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik except Hudayj; Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud is alone in transmitting it."
"4530","4524 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd al-A'raj, from az-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off the hand for a quarter of a dinar. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd al-A'raj except Ja'far ibn Sulayman."
"4531","4525 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Yahya al-Qarqasani narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammil ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution, then with it - and what a blessing; and whoever bathes, then bathing is better. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except Mu'ammil; Uthman ibn Yahya is alone in transmitting it."
"4532","4526 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym al-Juhani, he said: Our elders from Juhaynah narrated to us that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to them: Do not benefit from carrion in any way."
"4533","4527 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Abu Taybah, so he set the cupping instruments after sunset, then he ordered him at the fasting person's breaking of fast, and he cupped him. Then he asked him: How much is your tax? He said: Two sa's. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reduced a sa' for him. No one narrated this hadith from Ja'far ibn Burqan except Sa'id ibn Yahya; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"4534","4528 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition, and when the people came, among them was a man newly married. He hastened to his family and found his wife standing at her door, so he aimed the spear at her to stab her with it. She said: Do not hasten; look at what is in the house. He entered the house and found a snake coiled on its bed. He struck its head with the spear, and the snake did not die until the man died. That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: These houses have dwellers from the jinn. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing the house-snakes except the short-tailed one and the one with two stripes. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', with this wording except Yahya ibn Sulaym."
"4535","4529 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that az-Zubayr, on the morning of the Day of the Camel, bequeathed to [...]: There is no limb of my limbs except that it was wounded with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until that reached his private part. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except Qutaybah."
"4536","4530 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Abdur-Rahman ar-Ru'asi narrated to us, from al-Hasan al-Qassab, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding wiping over the leather socks: For the resident, a day and a night, and for the traveler, three days and their nights. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi' except al-Hasan al-Qassab."
"4537","4531 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Muhammad, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever breaks a fast day of Ramadan and dies before making it up, then for each day a mudd is due for a poor person. No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath except Abthar; and it is said that Muhammad from whom this hadith is narrated is Muhammad ibn Sirin, and it is said: Muhammad ibn Abi Layla."
"4538","4532 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Antaki narrated to us, he said: Ghusn ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Abu at-Tufayl, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of Tabuk, and he combined Zuhr with Asr, and Maghrib with Isha. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except Ghusn ibn Isma'il."
"4539","4533 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu at-Tufayl Amir ibn Wathilah, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he departed before the sun declined, would delay Zuhr until he prayed it with Asr; and when he departed after the sun declined, he would hasten Asr so as to pray them together; and when he departed before sunset, he would delay Maghrib so as to pray them together; and when he departed after sunset, he would pray it with Maghrib. This hadith is not narrated from Mu'adh ibn Jabal except with this chain; al-Layth ibn Sa'd is alone in transmitting it."
"4540","4534 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Muhammad ibn Abi Hakim, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the believer is like a tree whose leaves do not fall, neither in winter nor in summer. The people mentioned many trees, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the date-palm. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Abi Hakim except Abu al-Aswad; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"4541","4535 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Rizq ath-Thaqafi, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Shimasah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not accept Allah's concession, then upon him is sin like the mountains of Arafat. This hadith is not narrated from Uqbah ibn Amir except with this chain; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"4542","4536 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: ar-Rabi' ibn Badr narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield, as long as he does not tear it. It was said: And with what does he tear it? He said: With lying or backbiting."
"4543","4537 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Abu Ghatfan al-Murri, he said: I heard Abu al-Yasar ibn Amr al-Ansari saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship or treats him gently, Allah will shade him in His shade. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ghatfan except Abu al-Aswad; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"4544","4538 - Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from al-Walid ibn Ubadah, from Ubadah ibn as-Samit, that As'ad ibn Zurarah said: O people, do you know upon what you pledge allegiance to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? You pledge allegiance to him to fight Arabs and non-Arabs, jinn and men. They said: We are at war with whoever wars against us, and at peace with whoever makes peace with us. They said: O Messenger of Allah, stipulate. He said: You pledge allegiance to me to testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, to establish prayer, to give zakah, to hear and obey, not to dispute authority with its people, and to protect me as you protect yourselves and your families. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except Bahz ibn Asad; Qutaybah is alone in transmitting it."
"4545","4539 - Abdan ibn Ahmad al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar al-Bara narrated to us, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear his ring on his right hand. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Dinar except Abdur-Rahman ibn Ishaq, and no one narrated it from Abdur-Rahman except Abu Ma'shar; Abu Kamil is alone in transmitting it."
"4546","4540 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity on less than five uqiyahs, no charity on less than five awsuq, and no charity on less than five dhawd. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Hammad ibn Zayd; Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Hisab is alone in transmitting it."
"4547","4541 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Ubaydullah al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he saw a man of altered creation, would prostrate; when he saw a monkey, he would prostrate; and when he rose from his sleep, he would prostrate to Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except his son Yusuf; Abdur-Rahman ibn Ubaydullah is alone in transmitting it."
"4548","4542 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Iyad ibn Abdullah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Qatadah al-Ansari for the charity, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions went out in ihram until they stopped at Usfan, when they came upon a wild donkey. Abu Qatadah came while in a state of non-ihram, so they lowered their heads, disliking to point their gazes at it lest he notice. He saw it, mounted his horse, took the spear, and it fell from him. He said: Hand it to me. We said: We will not assist you against it in anything. He charged at it and hamstrung it. They began to roast from it, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is among us - he had gone ahead of them, so they caught up with him and asked him, and he saw no harm in it."
"4549","4543 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: One Umrah to the next Umrah is expiation for what is between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise."
"4550","4544 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Isa ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a small water-skin on the day of Uhud, so he urinated beside the water-skin, then drank from it. No one narrated these hadiths from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Abd al-A'la; Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uqayli and Abu Isa Abdullah ibn Unays are alone in transmitting them."
"4551","4545 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Zarbi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adam and Musa (peace be upon them) disputed with each other. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Bishr ibn Mansur; Ammar ibn Zarbi is alone in transmitting it."
"4552","4546 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Ubadi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn Salim al-Juhani narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Nafi', from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to me as a visitor, with no need driving him except visiting me, it is incumbent upon me to be an intercessor for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"4553","4547 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Ubadi narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn Salim al-Juhani narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Nafi', from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cupping in the head is a remedy for madness, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, and toothache."
"4554","4548 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Mihja' narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn Salim narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: A boy came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I intend this direction, for Hajj. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked with him and said: O boy, may Allah provide you with God-consciousness, direct you to good, and suffice you against worry. When the boy returned, he greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he raised his head to him and said: O boy, may Allah accept your Hajj, expiate your sin, and replace your expenditure."
"4555","4549 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Mihja' narrated to us, he said: Maslamah ibn Salim narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our freedmen are part of us. No one narrated these hadiths from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Maslamah ibn Salim."
"4556","4550 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn an-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Umar ibn Abdullah, from Bilal ibn al-Harith, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man utters a word pleasing to Allah without paying it any attention, and he is recorded thereby among the people of Allah's pleasure until the Day of Resurrection; and a man utters a word of Allah's wrath without paying it any attention, and he is recorded thereby among the people of His wrath until the day he meets Him. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Mu'tamir. And Umar ibn Abdullah is Ibn Utbah."
"4557","4551 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn an-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Abu an-Nadr, from Abu Salamah, from Aisha, she said: I would be sleeping with my feet in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he prayed at night; when he wanted to prostrate, he would strike my foot, so I would draw it in and he would prostrate. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Mu'tamir."
"4558","4552 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Junadah ibn Salm narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from Abdur-Rahman al-A'raj, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from Ali, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began prayer, he would say: I turn my face to the One who created the heavens and the earth, as a Hanif, a Muslim, and I am not among the polytheists. O Allah, You are the King, there is no god but You; glory and praise be to You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant; I confess my sin, so forgive all my sins, for none forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of morals, none guides to its best but You; avert its evil from me, none averts its evil but You. At Your service and blessed by You; all good is in Your hands, and I am by You and to You; there is no refuge from You except to You. Blessed and exalted are You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite. When he bowed, he would say: O Allah, to You I bow, to You I submit, in You I believe, and You are my Lord; my hearing, my sight, my bones, my marrow, and what my feet carry humble themselves to Allah, Lord of the worlds. When he raised his head, he would say: Allah hears whoever praises Him. Then he would say: Our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth, and filling whatever You will beyond that. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would prostrate, saying: O Allah, to You I prostrate, in You I believe, to You I submit, and You are my Lord; my face prostrates to the One who created it and fashioned its hearing and sight. Blessed is Allah, the Best of creators. Ubaydullah ibn Umar said: And Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah narrated to me, from Abdur-Rahman al-A'raj, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Junadah ibn Salm; Sahl ibn Uthman is alone in transmitting it."
"4559","4553 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Huraym ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik [...]. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Mu'tamir."
"4560","4554 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn an-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, she said: I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe from a single vessel, from janabah. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Mu'tamir."
"4561","4555 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: My uncle narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Ayyub as-Sakhtiyani, from Qatadah, from Musa ibn Salamah, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: We pray with you in the mosque, but when we pray in our dwellings we pray two rak'ahs? He said: That is the sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar; Ibn Wahb is alone in transmitting it."
"4562","4556 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Ma'iz ibn Malik came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: He committed adultery. He turned away from him, and he repeated it to him several times, and he turned away from him. He asked his people: Is he mad? They said: There is nothing wrong with him. He said: Did you do it with her? He said: Yes. So he ordered that he be stoned, and he was taken and stoned, and he did not pray over him. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Yazid ibn Zuray'; Abu Kamil is alone in transmitting it."
"4563","4557 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fosterage by a stray suckling does not make marriage unlawful. We said: What is al-ayfah? He said: A woman gives birth and milk congests in her breasts, so she suckles her neighbor woman once or twice. No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid except Sa'id ibn Yahya; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"4564","4558 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Hammad al-Ma'ni narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, I know it only from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Hunayn: Now the oven has heated up. Then he said: They are defeated, by the Lord of the Kaaba; they are defeated, by the Lord of the Kaaba. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Qurrah ibn Khalid, and no one narrated it from Qurrah except Abd al-A'la; Yusuf ibn Hammad is alone in transmitting it."
"4565","4559 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammil ibn Ihab narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammil ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb ... from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he is the truthful, the believed - narrated to us: The creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's womb for forty nights [...]."
"4566","4560 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us, he said: Jariyah ibn Harim narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Suwayd al-Adawi, from al-Ala ibn Ziyad, from Shaddad ibn Aws, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who, when morning comes and when evening comes, says: O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You; You created me and I am Your servant, and upon Your covenant as much as I can; I acknowledge Your blessing upon me, and I acknowledge my sins, so forgive my sins, for none forgives them but You - and dies that day, except that he enters Paradise; and if he dies that night, he enters Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Suwayd except Jariyah ibn Harim."
"4567","4561 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Uthman ibn Amr ibn Muslim ibn Amr ibn az-Zubayr ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Amr ibn Muslim ibn Amr narrated to me, he said: My grandfather Amr ibn az-Zubayr narrated to us, from his father az-Zubayr ibn Ubayd, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with three things: fasting three days of every month, bathing on Friday, and not sleeping except upon witr. Az-Zubayr said: I have not abandoned them since I heard them from Abu Hurayrah. And Amr said: I have not abandoned them since I heard them from my father. This hadith is not narrated from az-Zubayr except with this chain; Aban ibn Uthman is alone in transmitting it."
"4568","4562 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Amr ibn Harim, from Jabir ibn Zayd, he said: Abu Hurayrah claimed that he used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with Abu Bakr and Umar, from Madinah to Makkah; all of them prayed two rak'ahs from when they left Madinah until they returned to Madinah, while traveling and while staying in Makkah. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir ibn Zayd except with this chain; Abu Kamil al-Jahdari is alone in transmitting it."
"4569","4563 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Burd ibn Sinan, from Abu Harun, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: When we faced the enemy with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), each of us was more careful about his brother's knee when advancing in the row for fighting than about the arrow when shot, saying: Move your knee back, for I seek as you seek. Allah Almighty said: (As though they were a solid structure). No one narrated this hadith from Burd ibn Sinan except Isma'il ibn Ayyash; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"4570","4564 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Dawud al-Munkadiri narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, he said: Part of the sunnah of prayer is to erect his right foot and lay down the left. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Bakr ibn Sadaqah."
"4571","4565 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated to us, he said: Warqa ibn Umar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stopped at al-Hijr, said: Do not enter upon these punished people. Then he ordered the dough, and it was thrown away. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Warqa; Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi is alone in transmitting it."
"4572","4566 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabur ar-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a musk wallow, like the wallow of your beasts in this world. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Sabur is alone in transmitting it."
"4573","4567 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Hammad ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from al-Majishun, from Aisha, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was complaining, and I said: O my head. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What harm to you if that happens, and I stand over you and take care of you myself? I said: It is as if, if that happened, you would marry one of your wives. She said: I did not reach the evening of that day until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather I - O my head. Call for me your father and the men, for wishers will wish, but Allah and the believers refuse except Abu Bakr. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri, from al-Majishun - and he is Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah - except Sufyan ibn Husayn; Husayn ibn Numayr is alone in transmitting it."
"4574","4568 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn Abdullah an-Numayri Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Abu Sufyan al-Madini narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah, with Abu Bakr standing at his head, he said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, O Messenger of Allah, Abu Quhafah is a very old man in the outskirts of Makkah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rise with us to him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, he is more entitled to come to you. Abu Quhafah was brought, his beard and head like white thaghamah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change it, and avoid black."
"4575","4569 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn Abdullah an-Numayri narrated to us, he said: Abu Sufyan al-Madini narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Farahij, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer wrapped in a garment whose ends did not meet, so he knotted it. No one narrated these two hadiths from Dawud ibn Farahij except Abu Sufyan al-Madini."
"4576","4570 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: an-Nadr ibn Muhammad al-Jurashi narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a Muslim man says to his brother: O disbeliever, one of them returns with disbelief. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Ikrimah ibn Ammar; an-Nadr ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it, and Abdullah ibn Yazid is the freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan."
"4577","4571 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi ar-Rabi' as-Samman narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Among trees is a tree whose leaves do not fall, and it is the one likened to the believing servant. What is it? They began mentioning the trees of the valley. He said: It is the date-palm. Abdullah said: It occurred to me, but I was too shy to mention it."
"4578","4572 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi ar-Rabi' as-Samman narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah [...]. No one narrated these two hadiths from Zayd ibn Aslam except Sa'id ibn Salamah; Sa'id ibn Abi ar-Rabi' is alone in transmitting them."
"4579","4573 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, he said: Sughdi ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: Give every surah its due of bowing and prostration, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited only twenty surahs in ten rak'ahs."
"4580","4574 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, he said: Sughdi ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us a surah of the Quran, saying: Learn it, for there is no prayer except with tashahhud. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abu Hamzah except Sughdi ibn Sinan."
"4581","4575 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not swear by your fathers, nor by your mothers, nor by rivals to Allah; and do not swear by Allah except while truthful. No one narrated this hadith from Awf except Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh."
"4582","4576 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Khalifah ibn Khayyat al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Musa al-Juhani narrated to me, he said: al-Qasim ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets to mention Allah's name at the beginning of his food, let him say when he remembers: In the name of Allah, at its beginning and its end; for he begins fresh food, and prevents the wicked one from what he would take from it. No one raised this hadith from Musa al-Juhani except Umar ibn Ali; Shabab al-Usfuri is alone in transmitting it."
"4583","4577 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal ad-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Muhammad at-Tatari narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa Abu Dawud al-Kufi narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Marzuq, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people withhold zakah except that Allah afflicts them with years of drought. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Marzuq except Sulayman ibn Musa; Marwan ibn Muhammad at-Tatari is alone in transmitting it."
"4584","4578 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abu Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Talid ibn Sulayman Abu Idris narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from az-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, he said: al-Abbas and Ali came to Abu Bakr when he was made caliph, seeking their inheritance from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ali came seeking Fatimah's share, and al-Abbas came seeking his share of what was in the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Bakr said: I do not see that; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: We, the company of prophets, are not inherited from; what we leave is charity. A group of the Prophet's Companions stood and testified to that. They said: Leave it with us to be in our hands as it was in the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I do not see that; I am the guardian after him, and I am more entitled to that than you; I place it in the positions the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed it in. He refused to hand anything to them. When Umar became caliph, they came to him. He said: It is as if I am with Umar when wealth came to him, and he said: Take this wealth and distribute it among your people, when permission came to him. He said: At the door are people from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Admit them, and they entered and sat. Then he came to him and said: Ali and al-Abbas are at the door. He said: Admit them, and they entered. Umar said: What brings you? What you sought from Abu Bakr and he did not hand to you? They repeated it to him, and he said: I hand it to you on condition that I take from you a covenant and pledge that you act in it as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acted. Take it. He gave it to them and they took possession. Then they remained as long as Allah willed, then they disputed between themselves before Umar, with people from among the Prophet's Companions present. They disputed before him and said whatever Allah willed them to say. Some of the Prophet's Companions said: O Commander of the Believers, judge between them and relieve each of them of the other. Umar said: By Allah, I will never judge in it except the judgment I already judged; if you are unable over it, return it to me as I handed it to you. They rose from him. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Talid ibn Sulayman; Abu Musa al-Ansari is alone in transmitting it."
"4585","4579 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The disbeliever will be reckoned on the Day of Resurrection until sweat bridles him, until he says: O Lord, relieve me, even to the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, and no one narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except Yunus ibn Bukayr; Uqbah ibn Mukram is alone in transmitting it."
"4586","4580 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Abbas al-Uruzzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has not sent down to earth, from the creation of Adam until the Hour comes, a trial greater than the trial of the Dajjal. And I have said about him something no one before me said: He is short, curly-haired, with his left eye effaced, with a thick growth over his eye; he heals the blind and the leper, and says: I am your lord. Whoever says: My Lord is Allah, there is no trial upon him; and whoever says: You are my lord, is trialed. He remains among you as long as Allah wills, then Isa son of Maryam descends, affirming Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), upon his creed; he dies an guided imam and a just judge, and kills the Dajjal. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Muhammad ibn Marwan; Amr ibn al-Abbas is alone in transmitting it."
"4587","4581 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman, from Urwah ibn az-Zubayr, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from his father Zayd ibn Harithah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness to the mosques, of light on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith is not narrated from Zayd ibn Harithah except with this chain; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti is alone in transmitting it."
"4588","4582 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Yazid as-Suda'i narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Sulayman, from al-Haytham ibn Uqab, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leads people while among them is one who recites Allah's Book better than him, remains in baseness until the Day of Resurrection. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain; al-Husayn ibn Ali is alone in transmitting it."
"4589","4583 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Jawwas al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Burd ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Atiyah, the freedman of Salm ibn Ziyad, from Hudhayfah, raising it, he said: Trials come to you like pieces of dark night; a man wakes a believer and sleeps a disbeliever, and sleeps a believer and wakes a disbeliever; one of you sells his religion for a small portion of this world. I said: What do we do, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Break your hand. I said: If it heals? He said: Break the other. I said: If it heals? He said: Break your leg. I said: If it heals? He said: Break the other. I said: Until when? He said: Until a sinful hand or a decreed death comes to you. No one narrated this hadith from Burd ibn Sinan except Abthar ibn al-Qasim."
"4590","4584 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar and Duhaym narrated to us, they said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Janah narrated to us, from Ata ibn as-Sa'ib, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: I saw Umar ibn al-Khattab urinate and wipe his private part with dust, then turn to us and say: This is how we were taught. No one narrated this hadith from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Layla except Ata ibn as-Sa'ib, and no one narrated it from Ata except Rawh ibn Janah; al-Walid ibn Muslim is alone in transmitting it."
"4591","4585 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Utbah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik, saying: O Abu Hamzah, when one of us lends money and is given a gift? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you lends and is given a gift or carried on a mount, let him not accept it nor ride it, unless that was customary between them before. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Utbah ibn Humayd is alone in transmitting it."
"4592","4586 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was favored over those before me with five qualities: I was sent to all people, the red and the black; the earth was made for me a mosque and a means of purification; I was aided with awe for a month's journey; spoils were made lawful for me, and were not lawful for anyone before me; and it was said to me: Ask and you will be given, so I delayed my intercession for my ummah on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Salamah except Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, and no one narrated it from Ibn al-Munkadir except Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah; Isma'il ibn Ayyash is alone in transmitting it."
"4593","4587 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Nu'aym al-Mujmir and Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever strikes his slave for a prescribed crime he did not commit, his expiation is to free him. No one narrated this hadith from Nu'aym al-Mujmir and Salim except Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah; Isma'il ibn Ayyash is alone in transmitting it."
"4594","4588 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Yazid Abu Hazim al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Muslim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the wife of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas sought khul' from him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to observe a waiting period of one menstruation. No one connected this hadith from Ma'mar except Hisham ibn Yusuf."
"4595","4589 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: We used to count al-Ma'un as the axe, the pot, and the bucket. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Shayban; al-Walid ibn Muslim is alone in transmitting it."
"4596","4590 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed effeminate men and said: Expel them from your houses. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Hammad ibn Abdur-Rahman; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"4597","4591 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty is Modest and Generous; He is shy for His servant to raise his hands to Him and return them empty with nothing in them. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except his son Yusuf; Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"4598","4592 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Qatadah and Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes that Allah save him from the distresses of the Day of Resurrection and shade him under His Throne, let him grant respite to one in hardship. No one narrated this hadith from Sahl ibn Abi Salih except Isma'il ibn Ayyash."
"4599","4593 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Dahir ibn Nuh narrated to us, he said: Durust ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Hilal ibn Yazid, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Black seed is a remedy for every disease except as-sam. They said: What is as-sam, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Death. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Durust ibn Ziyad; Dahir ibn Nuh is alone in transmitting it."
"4600","4594 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the Mother of the Quran and Say: He is Allah, the One, it is as if he recited a third of the Quran. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Ahwal; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti is alone in transmitting it."
"4601","4595 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Duhaym al-Ma'wali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Marwan narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abu al-Mu'addil, that a man came to people while they were praying, with Ibn Umar sitting behind them on something, and said: O Abu Abdur-Rahman, what prevents you from praying? He said: I have already prayed, and we were forbidden to pray twice in one day. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Muhammad ibn Marwan; Duhaym al-Ma'wali is alone in transmitting it."
"4602","4596 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Musa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir, he said: The open spaces around the mosque became vacant, and Banu Salimah wanted to move near the mosque. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O Banu Salimah, stay in your homes; your footsteps are recorded for you. He said it three times. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud except Abd al-Warith; Imran ibn Musa is alone in transmitting it."
"4603","4597 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Dahir ibn Nuh narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Aradah narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abu al-Aliyah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three men set out and were caught by rain, so they took shelter in a cave. While they were in it, a rock tumbled from the heart of the mountain until it sealed the cave. The people said to one another: The rain has stopped, the trace is effaced, and no one has seen you but Allah; let each man look at the best deed he ever did and mention it, then supplicate to Allah. One of them said: O Allah, if You know that I was dutiful to my parents, bringing them their evening milk to drink, and one night I came to them with their evening milk and found them asleep in their beds - I disliked waking them from their sleep, and disliked returning with their evening milk before giving them to drink - and that remained my habit and theirs until dawn broke; if You know I was driven to that only by fear of You, then relieve us. It opened until light came in upon them. The other said: O Allah, I sought a woman and desired her, spending my wealth on her, until when I overcame her and sat from her as a man sits from a woman, she said to me: It is not lawful for you to break my seal except by its right. So I rose from her; if You know I was driven to that only by fear of You, then relieve us. The rock shifted and opened until, had the people wished to leave, they could have left. The other said: O Allah, if You know that I hired laborers who worked for me, and I paid them their wages except one man who left his wage until it multiplied into wealth; he came later seeking his wage, and I said to him: Take all of your wage; if You know I was driven to that by fear of You, then relieve us. The rock shifted and rolled away, and they went out embracing one another. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Abdullah ibn Aradah; Dahir ibn Nuh is alone in transmitting it."
"4604","4598 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Dahir ibn Nuh narrated to us, he said: Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn az-Zibriqan narrated to us, he said: Hudbah ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a woman prays her five, fasts her month, guards her chastity, and obeys her husband, she enters through whichever gates of Paradise she wishes. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Hudbah ibn al-Minhal, and no one narrated it from Hudbah except Abu Hammam; Dahir ibn Nuh is alone in transmitting it."
"4605","4599 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal ad-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Muhammad at-Tatari narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Jabir ibn Abdullah and al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A child does not inherit until he cries out at birth; his crying out is to scream, sneeze, or weep. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Marwan ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"4606","4600 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Humayd, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Aisha, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he would say: O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace; blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Utbah ibn Humayd; Isma'il ibn Ayyash is alone in transmitting it."
"4607","4601 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Khalid ad-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Muti' Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya informed me, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from the outskirts of Madinah intending prayer, and found the people had already prayed. He turned to his home, gathered his family, and prayed with them. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Abu Muti' Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, and it is not narrated from Abu Bakrah except with this chain."
"4608","Those named Ubaydullah. 4602 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari the judge narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from his father Ja'far, from his father, from his grandfather, from Husayn ibn Ali, from his father Ali ibn Abi Talib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reviles the prophets is killed, and whoever reviles my Companions is flogged. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Ibn Abi Uways is alone in transmitting it."
"4609","4603 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah al-Uwaysi narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A judge does not judge between two people except while satiated and quenched. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar is alone in transmitting it."
"4610","4604 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Atiq, from az-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir al-Madani - residing in al-Yamamah - he narrated to me that he heard Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman reporting from Aisha, that she said - and he raised it: He said: There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah; Ibn Abi Uways is alone in transmitting it."
"4611","4605 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Musa ibn Uqbah and Ibn Abi Atiq, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was in Paradise, I heard the voice of a man reciting the Quran. I said: Who is this? They said: This is Harithah ibn an-Nu'man. Such is dutifulness, such is dutifulness, such is dutifulness. And Harithah was among the most dutiful of people. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah and Ibn Abi Atiq except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Ibn Abi Uways is alone in transmitting it."
"4612","4606 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, that Abu ar-Raddad al-Laythi informed him, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Awf, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah said: I am ar-Rahman, and I created the womb-tie, deriving for it a name from My name; whoever joins it, I join him, and whoever severs it, I cut him off."
"4613","4607 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Atiq, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, that Abdullah ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: People are like a hundred camels among which you can hardly find a riding camel."
"4614","4608 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn Abdullah, that Abdullah ibn Umar used to walk in front of the funeral procession. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman used to walk in front of it."
"4615","4609 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Atiq, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, that he heard Hassan ibn Thabit al-Ansari calling Abu Hurayrah to witness, saying: O Abu Hurayrah, I ask you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Hassan, answer on behalf of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit?"
"4616","4610 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Atiq, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, that he saw upon Umm Kulthum, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a striped silk cloak."
"4617","4611 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr as-Salimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from his aunt, the daughter of Ka'b, from Furay'ah bint Malik, the sister of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, she informed her that she was under a man of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj; he went out seeking runaway slaves of his, overtook them at the edge of al-Qadum, and they attacked him and killed him. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking permission to leave my house, and he said: Until the decree reaches its term."
"4618","4612 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad as-Salimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah has not sent a prophet nor appointed a caliph except that he has two confidants: a confidant who commands him to good and forbids him from evil, and a confidant who does not spare him corruption. Whoever is protected from the evil confidant is protected."
"4619","4613 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate in prayer: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from sin and debt. They said: How often you seek refuge from debt? He said: When a man is in debt, he speaks and lies, and promises and breaks his promise."
"4620","4614 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ibn Abi Atiq, from Ibn Shihab, from Sinan ibn Abi Sinan ad-Du'ali, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion. A Bedouin stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, what of camels in the sand like gazelles ... ? He said: Then who infected the first?"
"4621","4615 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad as-Salimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways al-A'sha narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Bilal calls at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls."
"4622","4616 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad as-Salimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aisha, she said: The day of Ashura was a day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded fasting before Ramadan was made obligatory; then whoever wished fasted it, and whoever wished broke fast."
"4623","4617 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Sa'd ibn Ubadah to fulfill a vow that was upon his mother, who died before fulfilling it."
"4624","4618 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Atiq, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: that they used to eat the sacrificial animals in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for three days, not exceeding them, then after that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to eat and to take provision. No one narrated these hadiths from Ibn Abi Atiq and Musa ibn Uqbah except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways is alone in transmitting them."
"4625","4619 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi', from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, she said: Usamah ibn Zayd and Zayd ibn Harithah were together, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me joyful. I said: What is with you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Mujazziz just passed by Zayd and Usamah, saw their feet, and said: These feet are part of one another. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi', and no one narrated it from Ibn Mujammi' except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Ibn Abi Uways is alone in transmitting it."
"4626","4620 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah and Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he looked out from his house while the people were praying, raising their voices in recitation, and said to them: The one praying converses privately with his Lord, so let him consider what he converses with. Let none of you raise his voice over another with the Quran. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Abu Uways; his son Isma'il is alone in transmitting it."
"4627","4621 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Alqamah ibn Abi Alqamah, he said: Anas ibn Malik was asked about selling fruit? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it ripens. No one narrated this hadith from Alqamah except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Ibn Abi Uways is alone in transmitting it."
"4628","4622 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman al-Jud'ani narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Mirqa' al-Junda'i, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Calamity whitens the face of its bearer on the day faces blacken. Shu'ayb ibn Abdullah ibn Amr did not narrate from Ibn Abbas any hadith other than this; Ibn Abi Uways is alone in transmitting it."
"4629","4623 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik an-Nawfali narrated to me, from Abu Musa al-Hannat, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of the cupping in the middle of the head: Indeed it is against madness, leprosy, vitiligo, drowsiness, and molars, and he used to call it the rescuer. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri except with this chain; Ibn Abi Uways is alone in transmitting it."
"4630","4624 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, that men of the Ansar sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Permit us, O Messenger of Allah, to forgo the ransom of our nephew Abbas. He said: No, by Allah, you will not remit a dirham for him. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Musa ibn Uqbah."
"4631","4625 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah az-Zubaydi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad ad-Darawardi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from his uncle al-Harith ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Salamah, from Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of Aisha over women is like the excellence of tharid over food. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Dhi'b except ad-Darawardi; Ibrahim ibn Hamzah is alone in transmitting it."
"4632","4626 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Ya'qub ibn Abi Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Umar ibn Kathir ibn Aflah, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the lost item, that he used to say: O Allah, Returner of the lost, Guide of the misguided, You guide from misguidance; return my lost item to me by Your might and authority, for it is from Your gift and bounty. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Ibn Uyaynah; Abdur-Rahman ibn Ya'qub is alone in transmitting it, and this hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"4633","4627 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Uqayl, that he heard Sa'd ibn Ibrahim reporting, from Aisha bint Sa'd, that she narrated to him, from Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, she said: A Jewess entered upon me and spoke to me, saying in part of her speech: Yea, by the One who shields you from the trial of the grave. She said: I rebuked her and said: This is not the first of your lies about Allah and His Messenger; had there been torment of the grave, Allah would have informed His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of it. The Jewess said: We claim it has torment. Aisha said: When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, I informed him of her saying, but he returned nothing to me. After that he said: O Aisha, seek refuge in Allah from the torment of the grave; for had anyone been saved from it, Sa'd ibn Mu'adh would have been saved, but it was no more than a squeeze. No one narrated this hadith from Aisha bint Sa'd except Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, and no one narrated it from Sa'd except Uqayl; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"4634","4628 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by graves of women of Banu an-Najjar who died in Jahiliyyah, and heard them being tormented in the graves for tale-bearing. No one narrated this hadith from Usamah ibn Zayd except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"4635","4629 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Jubayr al-Hadhdha, that he heard Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf and Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Thawban reporting, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We attended a funeral with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he finished its burial and the people left, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He now hears the striking of your sandals. Munkar and Nakir come to him, their eyes like copper pots, their fangs like the horns of cattle, their voices like thunder. They sit him up and ask him what he worshipped and who his prophet was. If he was among those who worship Allah, he says: I worshipped Allah, and the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with clear proofs, so we believed and followed. That is Allah's saying: (Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in worldly life and in the Hereafter). It is said to him: Upon certainty you lived, upon it you died, and upon it you will be raised. Then a door to Paradise is opened for him, and his pit is widened. And if he was among the people of doubt, he says: I do not know; I heard people saying something, so I said it. It is said to him: Upon doubt you lived, upon it you died, and upon it you will be raised. Then a door to Hell is opened for him, and scorpions and snakes are unleashed upon him - had one of them breathed upon this world, nothing would grow - biting him; and the earth is commanded and compresses, until his ribs interlock. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl and Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Thawban except Musa ibn Jubayr; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it."
"4636","4630 - Ubaydullah ibn Rumahis al-Qaysi al-Jushami ar-Ramadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Amr Ziyad ibn Tariq - who had reached a hundred and twenty years - narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Jarwal Zuhayr ibn Surad saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took us captive on the day of Hunayn, the day of Hawazin, and began distributing the spoils and sheep, I recited to him this verse: Hazan. When he heard this verse, he said: What is mine and Banu Abd al-Muttalib's is yours. Quraysh said: What is ours belongs to Allah and His Messenger. And the Ansar said: What is ours belongs to Allah and His Messenger."
"4637","4631 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn as-Sannam ar-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Idris ibn Abi ar-Rabab narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while both were in ihram. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Hammad ibn Salamah; al-Hasan ibn Bilal is alone in transmitting it."
"4638","4632 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn as-Sannam ar-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus ar-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Artah ibn al-Mundhir, from Abu Amir al-Alhani, from Thawban, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will surely find peoples of my ummah coming on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds like the mountains of Tihamah, and Allah will make them scattered dust. They said: O Messenger of Allah, describe them to us lest we be among them without knowing. He said: They are your brothers, but they are peoples who, when alone with Allah's prohibitions, violate them."
"4639","4633 - Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Waqid Abu Shubayl narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Atiyah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most severely tormented of people on the Day of Resurrection is an unjust ruler. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Abu Hafs al-Abbar."
"4640","4634 - Ubaydullah ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Waqid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn Nafi' ad-Dabbi narrated to us, from Umar ibn Musa, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When the amen of the people of earth coincides with the amen of the people of heaven, he is forgiven. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Umar ibn Musa, and no one narrated it from Umar except Abd al-Jabbar ibn Nafi'; al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl is alone in transmitting it."
"4641","4635 - Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, Allah never sent down any revelation upon a prophet, between Him and him, except in Arabic, then he afterwards conveys it to his people in his own tongue. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Sulayman ibn Arqam; al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl was alone in narrating it."
"4642","4636 - Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, that he used to recite: (Our hearts are ghulf, burdened): vessels of wisdom. He said: The Jews said when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called them to learn wisdom: How can we learn when our hearts are but firmly sealed ghulf? That is: vessels of wisdom. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Sulayman ibn Arqam; al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl was alone in narrating it."
"4643","4637 - Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, who said: Two men of the Ansar recited a surah which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had taught them, and they used to recite it. One night they stood praying with it but could not recall a single letter of it. In the morning they came early to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned it to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are among what was abrogated and caused to be forgotten, so leave them alone. Al-Zuhri used to recite: {Whatever verse We abrogate or cause to be forgotten} with a dammah on the nun, light. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Sulayman ibn Arqam; al-Abbas was alone in narrating it."
"4644","4638 - Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from Humayd ibn Qays al-A'raj, from Mujahid: Ibn Abbas said regarding (There is no blame upon him to circumambulate them, heavily vowelled): whoever leaves it, there is no harm upon him. That reached Aishah, so she said: It is not as he said; had it been as he said it would have been: there is no blame upon him not to circumambulate them. Then she said: There were two idols upon al-Safa and al-Marwah in the pre-Islamic age, and they used to circumambulate between them. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) destroyed them as he destroyed the idols, the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt uneasy about circumambulating between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and said: We used to circumambulate because of the two idols, and Allah has destroyed them. So Allah sent down: {Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the rites of Allah}, meaning among the rites of Hajj, so do not feel uneasy about circumambulating between them."
"4645","4639 - Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Waqid narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Nafi' al-Dabbi, from Qatadah and Ja'far ibn Iyas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, regarding the statement of Allah: {And when they hear what was sent down to the Messenger, you see their eyes overflowing with tears}: He said: They were sailors - meaning seamen - who came with Ja'far ibn Abi Talib from Abyssinia. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the Quran to them, they believed and their eyes overflowed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps when you return to your land you will turn away from your religion. They said: We will never turn back from our religion, so Allah sent down that about their statement. This hadith was not narrated from Qatadah and Abu Bishr except by Abd al-Jabbar ibn Nafi'; al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl was alone in narrating it."
"4646","4640 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Shabib al-Qurashi al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Jazari narrated to us, saying: Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts Ramadan and six days of Shawwal has fasted the whole year. This hadith was not narrated from Rawh except by Makhlad ibn Yazid; al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub was alone in narrating it."
"4647","4641 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Shabib al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Salman ibn Abdullah al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise. This hadith was not narrated from al-Muharrar ibn Abi Hurayrah except by Ata; al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah was alone in narrating it."
"4648","4642 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Shabib al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Bakkar ibn al-Walid al-Dabbi narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Mazini narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas and Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six days of Shawwal has fasted the entire year. This hadith was not narrated from Amr ibn Dinar except by Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Mazini; Bakkar ibn al-Walid al-Dabbi, Abu al-Abbas ibn Bakkar, was alone in narrating it."
"4649","4643 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Khunays al-Dimyati narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Ata al-Balqawi narrated to us, saying: Hani ibn Abd al-Rahman and Rudayh ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, that they heard Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah say: I heard Umm al-Darda say: I heard Abu al-Darda say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says after the Fajr prayer, while his legs are still folded, before speaking: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise; He gives life and causes death; in His Hand is good, and He is over all things Capable - ten times - there is written for him for each time ten good deeds, and ten evil deeds are erased from him, and he is raised ten degrees, and they are for him on that day a guard against Satan the accursed and a guard against every harm. This hadith was not narrated from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah except by Hani ibn Abd al-Rahman and Rudayh ibn Atiyyah; Musa ibn Muhammad was alone in narrating it."
"4650","4644 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Khunays al-Dimyati narrated to us, saying: Abu Aslam Muhammad ibn Makhlad al-Ru'ayni al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Companions of the Heights (Ashab al-A'raf), so he said: They are men killed in the path of Allah while disobedient to their parents; their martyrdom prevented them from entering the Fire, and their disobedience prevented them from entering Paradise, so they are upon a wall between Paradise and the Fire until their flesh and fat waste away, until Allah finishes the reckoning of creation. When Allah finishes reckoning His creation and none remain but them, Allah envelops them in His mercy and admits them into Paradise by His mercy."
"4651","4645 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Khunays al-Dimyati narrated to us, saying: Abu Aslam Muhammad ibn Makhlad al-Ru'ayni narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: When news of the Negus's death came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Come out and pray over a brother of yours whom you have never seen. So we came out, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went forward and arranged us behind him, and he prayed and we prayed. When we left, the hypocrites said: Look at this one, he went out to pray over a Christian barbarian whom he never saw. So Allah sent down: {And indeed among the People of the Book are those who believe in Allah and what was sent down to you and what was sent down to them, humbling themselves before Allah, they do not sell the verses of Allah for a small price}, to the end of the verse."
"4652","4646 - Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Khunays al-Dimyati narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Makhlad al-Ru'ayni narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever drinks water on an empty stomach, his strength is diminished. These hadiths were not narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam except by his son Abd al-Rahman; Abu Aslam was alone in narrating them."
"4653","4647 - Ubaydullah ibn Ja'far ibn A'yan al-Baghdadi narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, saying: Asram ibn Hawshab narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Wasil al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far who said: Abbas came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I came to some people talking, and when they saw me they fell silent, and that was only because they found me burdensome. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did they really do that? By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, none of them believes until he loves you for my love; they hope to enter Paradise through my intercession, and the sons of Abd al-Muttalib do not hope for it."
"4654","4648 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, saying: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, saying: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, from Umm Habibah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: I was shown what my ummah will face after me, with some of them shedding the blood of others, and that was already decreed by Allah as it was decreed for the nations before you, so I asked Him to grant me my intercession on the Day of Resurrection for them, and He did. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Shu'ayb; Abu al-Yaman was alone in narrating it."
"4655","4649 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abu Mushir narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Yusuf al-Dimashqi narrated to us, saying: Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah who said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr led us in the Maghrib prayer and gave salam after two rak'ahs, then stood up to touch the Black Stone. The people said: Glory be to Allah. He turned to them and said: If only we had completed your prayer for you, but they gestured to him that he had not done so, so he returned, prayed the remaining rak'ah, then recited the tashahhud and gave salam, and prostrated two prostrations after giving salam. I went to Ibn Abbas and mentioned that to him, and he said: He did not deviate from the sunnah of his Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith was not narrated from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah except by Yazid ibn Yusuf; Abu Mushir was alone in narrating it."
"4656","4650 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer at three times: at sunrise until it rises, at midday, and at sunset. This hadith was not narrated from Yunus except by Ubaydullah ibn Amr."
"4657","4651 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, saying: Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ibn Abi Ishaq, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah informed him that Abu Bakrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling silver for silver except like for like, equal for equal, and selling gold for gold except like for like and equal for equal. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sell gold for silver however you wish, and silver for gold however you wish. This hadith was not narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except by Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam; Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi was alone in narrating it."
"4658","4652 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, saying: Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever persists stubbornly in an oath concerning his family is greater in sin. This hadith was not narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except by Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam."
"4659","4653 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, saying: Ufayr ibn Ma'dan narrated to us, saying: Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tale-bearing and malice are in the Fire; they do not both gather in the heart of a Muslim. This hadith was not narrated from Ata ibn Abi Rabah except by Ufayr ibn Ma'dan, and it is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"4660","4654 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says when he hears the call to prayer: By the right of this perfect call and the established prayer, grant Muhammad the Wasilah and the excellence, and raise him to the Praised Station which You promised him - intercession becomes due for him on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith was not narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except by Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah; Ali ibn Ayyash was alone in narrating it, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"4661","4655 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Ayyash and Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, saying: Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Aban ibn Uthman narrated to me, that he narrated to him, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever frees a believing slave, Allah frees every limb of him for every limb of her from the Fire. This hadith was not narrated from Sulayman ibn Yasar except by Abd al-Rahman ibn Aban; al-Attaf ibn Khalid was alone in narrating it."
"4662","4656 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, saying: Yunus ibn Uthman al-Muqri narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Sa'd, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends good for a servant, He sweetens him with honey. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how does He sweeten him? He said: He grants him success to do a righteous deed a year before his death, then takes his soul while upon it. This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain; Yahya ibn Salih was alone in narrating it."
"4663","4657 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, from Jabir, from Amir al-Sha'bi, from Zayd ibn Thabit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dictated to me this verse: {And We created man from an extract of clay} up to {then We produced him as another creation}. Mu'adh ibn Jabal said: So blessed be Allah, the Best of creators. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, so Mu'adh said to him: What are you laughing at, O Messenger of Allah? He said: With it was sealed {So blessed be Allah, the Best of creators}. This hadith is not narrated from Zayd ibn Thabit except with this chain; Adam was alone in narrating it."
"4664","4658 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, saying: Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Abdullah al-Sunabihi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Five prayers which Allah obligated upon His servants; whoever perfects their ablution, prays them at their times, and completes their bowing, prostration and humility, has a covenant from Allah that He will forgive him, and whoever does not do so has no covenant from Allah: if He wills He punishes him, and if He wills He forgives him. This hadith was not narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam except by Abu Ghassan and Hisham ibn Sa'd."
"4665","4659 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, saying: Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from Abu Bishr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Delaying payment by a rich man is injustice; if you are transferred to one who is solvent, accept the transfer; and do not approach the pregnant women among the captives until they give birth, and do not pay in advance for fruit until its owner is safe from loss. This hadith was not narrated from Habib ibn Ubayd except by Hariz ibn Uthman."
"4666","4660 - Abu Zur'ah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, saying: Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Habib ibn Ubayd, referring it to Abu Bishr, and Abu Bishr referring it to Aththamah ibn Qays al-Bajali, and Aththamah referring it to Abdullah ibn Sufyan al-Azdi, both of whom were Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no man who fasts a day in the path of Allah except that Allah distances him from the Fire by a hundred years. Habib said to Abu Bishr: Two hundred years? Abu Bishr said to Aththamah ibn Qays: I thought that. Abdullah ibn Sufyan said: I only narrate to you what I heard; I do not narrate to you what you narrate to me. This hadith was not narrated from Habib ibn Ubayd except by Hariz ibn Uthman, and it is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Sufyan al-Azdi except with this chain."
"4667","4661 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, saying: Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Shabib, that a Bedouin came to Abu Hurayrah and said: O Abu Hurayrah, narrate to us from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), repeating it to him three times, but Abu Hurayrah did not answer him, scratching with a stick of his without turning to him. When the Bedouin saw that, he turned away, so Abu Hurayrah said: Bring me the man. When he returned he said: Sit down. He said: A Bedouin like the other came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was scratching with a stick of his as you saw me scratching, and said: O Messenger of Allah, curse the people of Yemen, three times, and he was silent with him as I was with you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is this questioner who asked me to curse the people of Yemen? The man stood up to him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Faith is Yemeni, wisdom is Yemeni, and I find the breath of your Lord from the direction of Yemen. Verily disbelief, immorality and hardness of heart are among the loud-voiced herdsmen, the owners of hair and wool, whom Satan covers upon the rumps of camels. The man stood up angry, so he said: Return to me and I will add to you. This hadith was not narrated from Shabib except by Hariz ibn Uthman."
"4668","4662 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: Hariz ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Sulayh al-Rahabi narrated to me, referring it to Dhu Mikhmar, who used to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he heard him say: We were in an expedition with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he turned back, hastening the march, and nothing made him do that except scarcity of provisions. The people became cut off behind him, so someone said: O Messenger of Allah, the people have been cut off behind you. He sat until they caught up with him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or someone - said: Would you like to rest a rest? They agreed to that, and the people dismounted. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will guard us tonight? Dhu Mikhmar said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. He gave him the halter of his she-camel and said: Do not be a luk'a (worthless weakling). I went off not far, holding the halter of the Prophet's she-camel and my own she-camel, then I let them graze. My eyes overcame me, and nothing woke me but the heat of the sun on my face. I looked right and left, frightened, and there were the two mounts not far away. I took them, then came to the nearest people and woke him, then asked him: Did you pray? He said: No. People woke one another until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke up and said: O Bilal, is there water in the container? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He brought the ablution vessel, and he performed ablution thoroughly without leaving dust from it, then said: O Bilal, call the adhan - while being unhurried. He called the adhan, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr unhurriedly, then ordered Bilal, who established the prayer, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed unhurriedly. Someone said: O Prophet of Allah, did we fall short? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, Allah took our souls then returned them to us, and we prayed."
"4669","4663 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The last of the two rulings from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was abandoning ablution for what was touched by fire. This hadith is not narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except by Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah; Ali ibn Ayyash was alone in narrating it."
"4670","4664 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Fudayl ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Hanafi narrated to us, saying: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a month before his death, and he wiped over the leather socks and the turban. This hadith was not narrated from Sulayman al-Taymi except by Ali ibn al-Fudayl."
"4671","4665 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Jumahir Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Habib ibn Abi al-Ishrin narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst thief among people is the one who steals his prayer. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does he steal it? He said: He does not complete its bowing nor its prostration. This hadith was not narrated from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except by Ibn Abi al-Ishrin."
"4672","4666 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Amr ibn Dinar al-Makki, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There will be a tribulation in which one side does not calm down except another side surges, until a caller calls from the sky: Your leader is so-and-so. This hadith is not narrated from Talhah except with this chain; Isma'il ibn Ayyash was alone in narrating it."
"4673","4667 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn A'idh narrated to us, saying: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from al-Mut'im ibn al-Miqdam, from Mujahid who said: I went out on a military expedition with a companion, and Abdullah ibn Umar saw us off. When he was about to part from us he said: I have no wealth to give you, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah is entrusted with something, He preserves it, and I entrust to Allah your religion, your trusts, and the seals of your deeds. This hadith was not narrated from al-Mut'im except by Ibn Humayd."
"4674","4668 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Musa al-Dimashqi narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drags his garments out of pride, Allah will not look at him. Abu Rayhanah said: By Allah, what you narrated to us has made me ill, for by Allah I love beauty so much that I put it even in the strap of my sandal and the loop of my whip - is that pride? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty, and loves to see the trace of His blessing upon His servant. But pride is: rejecting the truth and despising people. This hadith was not narrated from Ata al-Khurasani except by Isa ibn Musa; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman was alone in narrating it."
"4675","4669 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no protected pasture except for Allah and His Messenger. This hadith was not narrated from Abu al-Zinad except by Shu'ayb; Ali ibn Ayyash was alone in narrating it."
"4676","4670 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Salamah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Successful is the one who submits, whose provision is sufficient, and who is patient with that."
"4677","4671 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us, saying: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Ghaylan narrated to me, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah who said: I was with Abdullah ibn Umar, and he said: I was one of ten in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Ibn Mas'ud, Ibn Jabal, Hudhayfah, Ibn Awf, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and myself. A young man of the Ansar came, gave salam, then sat and said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the believers is best? He said: The best of them in character. He said: Which of the believers is most prudent? He said: Those who remember death most and prepare best before it befalls them; those are the prudent. Then the youth fell silent, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to us and said: O company of Emigrants, five traits: if you are tested with them and they befall you - and I seek refuge with Allah that you reach them: indecency never appears among a people until they declare it openly except that plague and pains appear among them such as never occurred among their predecessors who passed; they never diminish the measure and scale except they are seized by years of drought, severity of provision, and tyranny of rulers over them; they never withhold the zakah of their wealth except they are denied rain from the sky, and were it not for the animals they would not be rained upon; they never break the covenant of Allah and His Messenger except Allah gives their enemy power over them, then they invade them and take some of what was in their hands; and they do not judge by the Book of Allah except Allah sets their violence among themselves. Then he ordered Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, who prepared for an expedition he sent him upon. In the morning he had wrapped himself in a black cotton turban, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him, undid it, turbaned him and let loose four fingers behind him, saying: Wrap thus, O Ibn Awf, for it is more recognizable and better. Then he ordered Bilal, who handed him the banner, and he praised Allah and invoked blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then said: Take it, O Ibn Awf, and fight all together in the path of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah; do not betray, do not mutilate; this is the covenant of Allah and the sunnah of your Prophet among you."
"4678","4672 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, saying: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik who said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If only you would visit Abdullah ibn Ubayy. He set out to him riding his donkey, with some of his Companions. When they reached him, Abdullah ibn Ubayy said: Keep away, for the stench of your donkey has harmed me. A Muslim man said: By Allah, the donkey of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smells sweeter than you. A man of his people became angry on behalf of Abdullah, and one of them became angry on behalf of his people, and there was fighting with palm stalks and sandals. We were told that this verse was sent down concerning them: {And if two parties of the believers fight, make peace between them}."
"4679","4673 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, saying: Salamah ibn Kulthum narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a funeral, pronouncing takbir four times over it, then came to the grave and threw three handfuls of earth upon it from the head side. This hadith was not narrated from al-Awza'i except by Salamah ibn Kulthum; Yahya ibn Salih was alone in narrating it."
"4680","4674 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ala ibn Zibr narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the night prayer, so he said: Two by two; when you fear dawn will overtake you, pray witr with one."
"4681","4675 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, saying: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, from Ibn Umar who said: We went in the morning with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Mina to Arafat, some of us saying the talbiyah and some saying the takbir."
"4682","4676 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Junadah ibn Muhammad al-Murri narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Habib ibn Abi al-Ishrin narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: You will surely be sifted as dates are sifted from refuse; your best will depart and your worst will remain; if you are able to die, then die."
"4683","4677 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Asbagh ibn Muhammad, nephew of Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Raqqi, narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world will not pass away until a worthless son of a worthless one rules it, and the best of people is a believer between two noble ones. This hadith is not narrated from Umar except with this chain; Asbagh ibn Muhammad, nephew of Ubaydullah ibn Amr, was alone in narrating it."
"4684","4678 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The left side of the mosque has been left unused. He said: Whoever keeps the left side of the mosque inhabited shall have a double share of reward. This hadith was not narrated from Nafi' except by Layth, nor from Layth except by Ubaydullah ibn Amr; Amr ibn Uthman was alone in narrating it."
"4685","4679 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ata, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken up, I passed by the highest assembly, with Gabriel like a worn-out rug from fear of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Karim except by Ubaydullah ibn Amr."
"4686","4680 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Sumay', from Muslim al-Batin, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever makes a show, Allah will make a show of him; whoever shows off, Allah will show him off. This hadith was not narrated from Isma'il ibn Sumay' except by Hafs ibn Ghiyath; his son was alone in narrating it."
"4687","4681 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and Abu al-Aliyah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt or maternal aunt. This hadith was not narrated from Qatadah, from Abu al-Aliyah, except by Sa'id ibn Bashir; Muhammad ibn Bakkar was alone in narrating it."
"4688","4682 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would avoid the gush of blood for three days, then be intimate afterwards. This hadith was not narrated from Qatadah except by Sa'id ibn Bashir; Muhammad ibn Bakkar was alone in narrating it."
"4689","4683 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Hafs narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade selling what one does not own - what is not with you - and profit from what was not guaranteed, and a sale combined with a loan, and a sale containing two conditions, saying: This is for such-and-such in cash, and for such-and-such on credit. This hadith was not narrated from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz except by Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb."
"4690","4684 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ibrahim, from Shurayh, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your children are of your earnings, and the best you eat is of your earnings. This hadith was not narrated from Matar except by Sa'id ibn Bashir."
"4691","4685 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed five rak'ahs, then prostrated two prostrations. This hadith was not narrated from Mansur ibn Zadham except by Sa'id ibn Bashir."
"4692","4686 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss one of his wives, then go out to prayer without performing ablution. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Mansur; Sa'id ibn Bashir was alone in narrating it."
"4693","4687 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Ghasil narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Sahl ibn Sa'd who said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr say upon the pulpit of Makkah: O people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would love to have a second to it; if given a second, he would love a third to it; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns to whoever repents. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr except with this chain; Abu Nu'aym was alone in narrating it."
"4694","4688 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, saying: Mindal narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married together with her paternal aunt, nor with her maternal aunt. This hadith was not narrated from al-A'mash except by Mindal; Muhammad ibn al-Salt was alone in narrating it."
"4695","4689 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, saying: Abu Kudaynah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Duha, from Ibn Abbas who said: A Jew passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O Jew, tell us. He said: What do you say, O Abu al-Qasim, when Allah places the heaven upon this finger, the earth upon this finger, the mountains upon this finger, the seas upon this finger, and the rest of creation upon this finger? He said: So Allah sent down: {And they did not esteem Allah with His true estimation}. This hadith was not narrated from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu al-Duha, from Ibn Abbas, except by Abu Kudaynah; Muhammad ibn al-Salt was alone in narrating it."
"4696","4690 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id and Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of this plant must not approach our mosque - meaning garlic. This hadith was not narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam and Yahya ibn Sa'id except by Isma'il ibn Ayyash; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman was alone in narrating it."
"4697","4691 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Daws al-Shami narrated to us, saying: A man called Abu Ma'qil came and said to me: Write. So I wrote: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. He said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: My close friend Abu al-Qasim, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), advised me with three things - may my father and mother be sacrificed for him: fasting three days of every month, sleeping upon witr, and the forenoon glorification. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Ma'qil except by Abu al-Daws; Abu Nu'aym was alone in narrating it."
"4698","4692 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Jumahir Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Allah, place in our land its blessing, its adornment, and its tranquility. This hadith was not narrated from Matar al-Warraq except by Sa'id ibn Bashir."
"4699","4693 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Jumahir Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Abu Ka'b Ayyub ibn Musa al-Sa'di narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Habib al-Muharibi, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I am a guarantor of a house in the outskirts of Paradise for whoever abandons argument even if he is right, and a house in the middle of Paradise for whoever abandons lying even in jest, and a house in the highest part of Paradise for whoever has good character. This hadith was not narrated from Sulayman ibn Habib except by Abu Ka'b."
"4700","4694 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated to us, saying: al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah's anger is severe against a woman who brings into a people one who is not of them, to share with them in their wealth and to look upon their private matters. This hadith was not narrated from Ayyub ibn Musa except by Ibrahim ibn Yazid, nor from Ibrahim except by al-Mu'afa; al-Hasan ibn Bishr was alone in narrating it."
"4701","4695 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Muslim al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Most High said: Might is My cloak and pride is My lower garment; whoever contends with Me for either of them, I will punish him. This hadith was not narrated from al-A'mash except by Hafs."
"4702","4696 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Sawwar ibn Umarah al-Ramli narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the believer among the people of faith is like the head to the body: he feels pain for what befalls the people of faith as the head feels pain for what befalls the body. This hadith was not narrated from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad except by Sawwar ibn Umarah."
"4703","4697 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Junadah ibn Abi Khalid, from Makhul, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu al-Darda who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever walks in the darkness of night to the mosques, Allah will grant him light on the Day of Resurrection."
"4704","4698 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile night and day, nor the sun, nor the moon, nor the wind, for they are a mercy to some people and a punishment to others. This hadith was not narrated from Abu al-Zubayr except by Sa'id ibn Bashir; Muhammad ibn Bakkar was alone in narrating it."
"4705","4699 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not accompany a caravan in which there is a bell, nor a house in which there is a bell. This hadith was not narrated from Abu al-Zubayr except by Sa'id ibn Bashir; Muhammad ibn Bakkar was alone in narrating it."
"4706","4700 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Sawwar ibn Umarah al-Ramli narrated to us, saying: Masarrah ibn Ma'bad al-Lakhmi narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Abi Kabshah led us in Asr prayer, then turned to us after his salam and informed us that he had prayed behind Marwan ibn al-Hakam, who prostrated with us like these two prostrations. Then Marwan said: I prayed behind Uthman ibn Affan, who prostrated with us like these two prostrations. Then Uthman said: I was with your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, I prayed and did not know whether I prayed an even or odd number, then I prayed and did not know whether I prayed even or odd - saying it three times. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) answered him, saying: Satan plays with you in your prayer; whoever prays and does not know whether he prayed even or odd, let him prostrate two prostrations, for they complete his prayer. This hadith was not narrated from Masarrah ibn Ma'bad except by Sawwar ibn Umarah, and it is not narrated from Uthman except with this chain."
"4707","4701 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abu Mushir narrated to us, saying: al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Asid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Khalid ibn Durayk, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How will you be when some of you kill others? They said: Today some of us already kill others? He said: That is not what I mean, but the killing of Muslims by one another, when the minds of men are taken away and they deem error to be guidance. This hadith was not narrated from al-Awza'i except by al-Hiql."
"4708","4702 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Mu'adh ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I do a deed which is seen and it pleases me? He said: You have two rewards: the reward of secrecy and the reward of openness. This hadith was not narrated from Sa'id ibn Bashir except by Muhammad ibn Bakkar and Muhammad ibn Mu'adh."
"4709","4703 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn A'idh narrated to us, saying: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, from Hayyan ibn Hujr, from Abu al-Ghadiyah al-Muzani who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be severe, harsh tribulations; the best people in them will be the Muslims of the desert dwellers, who do not covet anything of people's blood or wealth."
"4710","4704 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he asked about a man's name, if it was good it would be recognized on his face, and if it was bad it would be seen on his face; and when he asked about the name of a town, likewise. This hadith was not narrated from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, except by Sa'id ibn Bashir; Yahya ibn Salih was alone in narrating it. Hisham al-Dastuwa'i narrated it from Qatadah, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father."
"4711","4705 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The severest regrets of the sons of Adam are over three: a man who had a beautiful wife who pleased him, she bore him a boy then died, and he has nothing with which to hire a wet-nurse for him; a man on a horse in battle who saw booty and raced his companions to it, and when he neared it his horse fell and died, so he was beaten to the booty; and a man who had crops and a water-carrying camel, and when his crops ripened and pleased him, his camel died and he has nothing with which to buy a camel, so his crops died. This hadith was not narrated from Qatadah except by Sa'id ibn Bashir."
"4712","4706 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Abu Hubayrah Yahya ibn Abbad, from his grandfather Shayban who said: I entered the mosque and sat by a room, then cleared my throat. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu Yahya, come to lunch. I said: I am fasting. He said: I too intended to fast, but our caller to prayer called before dawn broke, and there is something wrong with his eyes. This hadith was not narrated from Ash'ath except by Hafs."
"4713","4707 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr and Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, my wife does not repel the hand of one who touches? He said to him: Divorce her. He said: I love her. He said: Then enjoy her. This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Karim except by Ubaydullah and Musa ibn A'yan."
"4714","4708 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, saying: Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on a servant who is easy when he pays, easy when he collects. This hadith was not narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except by Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif."
"4715","4709 - Abu Zur'ah narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak al-Suri narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Dawud, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, that he went to the mosque of Damascus early in the forenoon, and met Shaddad ibn Aws with al-Sunabihi with him. I said: Where are you going, may Allah have mercy on you both? They said: We intend here to visit a sick brother of ours. I went with them until we entered upon that man, and they said: How are you this morning? He said: I am in Allah's blessing and favor. Shaddad said: Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: When I afflict a believing servant of Mine, and he praises Me and is patient with what I afflicted him with, he rises from that bed as on the day his mother bore him, free of sins, and the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says to the guardian angels: I restrained this servant of Mine and afflicted him, so record for him what you used to record for him of reward before that while he was healthy. This hadith is not narrated from Shaddad except with this chain; Isma'il ibn Ayyash was alone in narrating it."
"4716","4710 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ru'asi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Hakim Abu Bakr al-Dahiri narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Shami, from Isma'il ibn Ubaydullah, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The feet of a servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about four: his youth, how he spent it; his life, how he consumed it; his wealth, whence he earned it and wherein he spent it. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Darda except with this chain."
"4717","4711 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Aban ibn Salih, from Mujahid Abu al-Hajjaj, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah created mercy as one hundred mercies; He kept ninety-nine mercies with Him and placed one mercy among all His creation. If the disbeliever knew all that is with Allah of mercy, he would not despair of Paradise; and if the believer knew all that is with Allah of punishment, he would not feel safe from the Fire. This hadith was not narrated from Mujahid except by Aban ibn Salih, nor from Aban except by Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal."
"4718","4712 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Faith has sixty-four doors - or sixty-four branches - the highest of them is There is no god but Allah, and the lowest is removing harm from the path. This hadith was not narrated from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah except by Abu Bakr ibn Mudar. Sufyan al-Thawri, Ibn Ajlan and others narrated it from Sahl ibn Abi Salih, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4719","4713 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, saying: Abu Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-San'ani narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my ummah. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman; Abu al-Tahir was alone in narrating it."
"4720","4714 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, saying: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, from Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A life-grant (umra) is like inheritance. This hadith was not narrated from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub except by Rawh ibn Salah."
"4721","4715 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Ufayr narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Any woman who fears her Lord, guards her chastity, and obeys her husband, eight doors of Paradise are opened for her, and it is said to her: Enter from whichever you wish. This hadith was not narrated from Musa ibn Wardan except by Ibn Lahi'ah."
"4722","4716 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, saying: Rawh ibn Salah narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you fights, let him avoid the face. This hadith was not narrated from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub except by Rawh ibn Salah."
"4723","4717 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Muhammad al-Balqawi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Marwan al-Suddi narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek bounty from the merciful of my ummah, live in their care, and do not seek it from the hard-hearted, for they await My anger. This hadith was not narrated from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except by Muhammad ibn Marwan; Musa ibn Muhammad was alone in narrating it."
"4724","4718 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Yahya ibn al-Nadr, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, if modesty were a man it would be a righteous man, and if obscenity were a man it would be an evil man. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Salamah except by Yahya ibn al-Nadr, nor from Yahya ibn al-Nadr except by Abu al-Aswad; Ibn Lahi'ah was alone in narrating it."
"4725","4719 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik, from Maymun ibn Mihran who said: I visited Safiyyah bint Shaybah - an elderly woman - and said to her: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marry Maymunah while in ihram? She said: No; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while they were both lawful (not in ihram). This hadith was not narrated from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Safiyyah, except by Abd al-Karim; Ubaydullah ibn Amr was alone in narrating it."
"4726","4720 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated to me, saying: Qatadah ibn Di'amah al-Basri narrated to me, from al-Hasan, from Thawban, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The cupper and the one cupped both break their fast. This hadith was not narrated from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Thawban, except by al-Layth ibn Sa'd."
"4727","4721 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abu Salih al-Samman, from Abu Dharr, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was delivering a sermon, and sat down. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Dharr: Did you bow? He said: No. He said: Stand and bow. He stood and bowed two rak'ahs. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Did you seek refuge in them from the evil of the devils of jinn and men? I said: O Messenger of Allah, who was the first of the prophets? He said: Adam. I said: Was he a prophet? He said: Yes, one spoken to. I said: Then who? He said: Noah, and between them ten forefathers. I said: Then who? He said: Ibrahim, and between them ten forefathers. I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about prayer. He said: Good spread out; whoever wishes may take much of it. I said: What is charity? He said: Multiplied manifold. I said: What is fasting? He said: Fasting is a shield; Allah said: Fasting is Mine and I reward for it. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk. I said: Which charity is best? He said: The striving of one with little, and a secret gift to a poor person. I said: Which necks (slaves to free) are best? He said: The most expensive in price. This hadith was not narrated from Safwan ibn Sulaym except by Khalid ibn Yazid; Ibn Lahi'ah was alone in narrating it."
"4728","4722 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah al-Utbi narrated to us, saying: Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, saying: Abthar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Burd ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, saying: Abu Sufanah al-Nakha'i narrated to me, from Aishah, that she used to scrape semen from the garment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith was not narrated from Abu Sufanah except by Burd ibn Abi Ziyad; Abthar ibn al-Qasim was alone in narrating it."
"4729","4723 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'dan ibn Jum'ah al-Ta'i al-Ladhiqi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah al-Uwaysi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salam. This hadith was not narrated from Abdullah ibn Umar except by Abd al-Aziz al-Uwaysi."
"4730","4724 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'dan ibn Jum'ah al-Ladhiqi narrated to us, saying: Mutarrif ibn Abdullah al-Madani narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sees an afflicted person, let him say: Praise be to Allah who favored me over him and over many of His servants with favor; when he says that, he has thanked for that blessing. This hadith was not narrated from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih except by Abdullah ibn Umar; Mutarrif ibn Abdullah was alone in narrating it."
"4731","4725 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatim Abu Zayd al-Muradi al-Misri narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Ufayr and Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, saying: Amir ibn Yahya al-Ma'afiri narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah will single out a man of my ummah who has ninety-nine scrolls, each scroll as far as the eye can see, and say to him: Do you deny any of this? Did My recording scribes wrong you? He will say: No, my Lord. He will say: Rather, you have a good deed with Us, and there is no wrong upon you today. A card is brought out for him containing: I testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He will say: Attend your weighing. He will say: What is this card compared to these scrolls? The card will outweigh, and nothing outweighs the name of Allah. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Amir ibn Yahya was alone in narrating it."
"4732","4726 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatim al-Muradi narrated to us, saying: Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No earner has earned anything like the excellence of knowledge that guides its owner to guidance or turns him away from ruin; and his religion is not upright until his intellect is upright. This hadith was not narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam except by his son Abd al-Rahman; Asbagh ibn al-Faraj was alone in narrating it."
"4733","4727 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatim al-Muradi narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Urwah, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zaynab is the best of my daughters; she was afflicted through me. That reached Ali ibn Husayn, so he came to him and said: What is this report reaching me from you in which you belittle Fatimah? Urwah said: I would not love to have such-and-such in return for belittling Fatimah; it is truly hers. As for after this, I owe you never to narrate it again. This hadith was not narrated from Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Urwah except by Yazid ibn al-Had."
"4734","4728 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn narrated to us, saying: I bear witness upon my father, that he narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I came forth from marriage, not from fornication, from Adam until my father and mother bore me. This hadith was not narrated from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad except by Muhammad ibn Abi Umar."
"4735","4729 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, saying: al-Husayn ibn al-Zibriqan al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sinan, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels continue to invoke blessings upon one of you as long as his dining spread remains laid out. This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain; Mindal ibn Ali was alone in narrating it."
"4736","4730 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to kiss her while fasting. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Isma'il ibn Muslim; Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman was alone in narrating it."
"4737","4731 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They pray for one of you as long as he remains in his place of prayer, as long as he does not break his ablution: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him."
"4738","4732 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer. These two hadiths were not narrated from Hisham ibn Urwah except by Uqbah ibn Khalid; Sahl ibn Uthman was alone in narrating them."
"4739","4733 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Abu Ya'qub al-Thaqafi who said: Yunus ibn Ubayd, freedman of Muhammad ibn al-Qasim, narrated to me, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim sent me to al-Bara ibn Azib to ask him about the banner of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), what was it? He said: It was black, square, made of Namirah cloth. This hadith is not narrated from al-Bara ibn Azib except with this chain; Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah was alone in narrating it."
"4740","4734 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, from Umm Salamah who said: Before he died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would often say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I see you often saying: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. He said: I was commanded with a command, then he recited: {When the help of Allah and victory come}. This hadith was not narrated from Asim except by Hafs; Sahl ibn Uthman was alone in narrating it."
"4741","4735 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he heard the call to prayer, would say: And I, and I. This hadith was not narrated from Hisham except by Hafs and Ali ibn Mushir; Sahl ibn Uthman was alone in narrating it."
"4742","4736 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Hashim ibn Marzuq narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The ring of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of silver, its stone of silver. This hadith was not narrated from Asim except by Amr ibn Abi Qays."
"4743","4737 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Layth, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The son of Adam was commanded to prostrate upon seven bones. One of them said: And not to gather hair nor garment. This hadith was not narrated from Ubayd ibn Umayr except by Abu al-Zubayr, nor from Abu al-Zubayr except by Layth, nor from Layth except by Hafs; Sahl was alone in narrating it."
"4744","4738 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Mahmud ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Urwah al-Bariqi, that he would drive his horse before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessed be Allah, how beautiful are their hooves and their lower legs? This is not narrated from Urwah al-Bariqi except with this chain; Mahmud ibn Ghaylan was alone in narrating it."
"4745","4739 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Sulaym ibn Mansur ibn Ammar narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Malik al-Nawfali narrated to us, saying: Abu Ubadah al-Zuraqi narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The funeral of Jabir ibn Atik was brought - or he said: Sahl ibn Atik - and he was the first over whom prayer was offered in the funeral place. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward, pronounced takbir, recited the Mother of the Quran aloud, then pronounced the second takbir and prayed for himself and the Messengers, then pronounced the third takbir and supplicated for the deceased, saying: O Allah, forgive him, have mercy on him, and raise his rank. Then he pronounced the fourth takbir and supplicated for the believing men and women, then gave salam. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Abu Ubadah al-Zuraqi, nor from Abu Ubadah except by Yahya ibn Yazid; Sulaym ibn Mansur was alone in narrating it."
"4746","4740 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When I take the two precious things of a servant - and he is patient and reckons reward - his recompense is Paradise. This hadith was not narrated from Muhammad ibn Amr except by Ali ibn Mushir; Sahl ibn Uthman was alone in narrating it."
"4747","4741 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Ziyad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Khaythamah, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves to be moved away from the Fire and admitted into Paradise, let death come to him while he testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and let him treat people as he loves to be treated. This hadith was not narrated from Talhah ibn Musarrif except by Layth, nor from Layth except by Ziyad ibn Abdullah; Sahl ibn Uthman was alone in narrating it, and it is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr except with this chain."
"4748","4742 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Layth, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Umm Dharrah, from Aishah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I and the guardian of an orphan - his own or another's - are in Paradise, and the one who strives for the widow and the poor is like the warrior in the path of Allah. This hadith was not narrated from Umm Dharrah except by Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, nor from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except by Layth, nor from Layth except by Hafs; Sahl ibn Uthman was alone in narrating it."
"4749","4743 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, that some women of Hims entered upon Aishah, and she said: Perhaps you are among the women who enter bathhouses? They said to her: We do that. Aishah said to them: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any woman who removes her clothes in other than her husband's house tears what is between her and Allah. This hadith was not narrated from Ata except by Yazid, nor from Yazid except by Imran ibn Uyaynah."
"4750","4744 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, saying: Qabisah ibn Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Umm Thaljah who said: I visited Aishah, and a man called to her from behind the veil, asking her about nabidh. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gourds and pitch-coated vessels. This hadith was not narrated from Umm Thaljah except by Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, nor from Yazid except by Qabisah ibn Layth; Muhammad ibn Ubayd was alone in narrating it."
"4751","4745 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Razi narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Abd al-Malik, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Dabbah ibn Mihsan al-Asadi, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There will be rulers over you whom you recognize and disapprove of; whoever disapproves has freed himself, and whoever hates has become safe, but whoever is pleased or follows. She said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not kill them? He said: No, as long as they establish prayer. This hadith was not narrated from Ash'ath ibn Abd al-Malik except by Muhammad ibn al-Mu'alla."
"4752","4746 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Thabit Farkhawayh al-Razi narrated to us, saying: al-Ala ibn Hilal al-Raqqi narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever clips his nails on Friday is protected from evil until the like thereof. This hadith was not narrated from Ayyub except by Yazid ibn Zuray', nor from Yazid ibn Zuray' except by al-Ala ibn Hilal; Farkhawayh was alone in narrating it."
"4753","4747 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: al-Husayn ibn Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated to us, saying: al-Walid ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Musa narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father who said: The recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with prolongation, without warbling."
"4754","4748 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: al-Husayn ibn Isa ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, saying: Abu Zuhayr Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Kurayb narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does he steal while he is a believer, nor does he plunder a booty while the believers raise their heads to it while he is a believer. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah, except by Kurayb, nor from Kurayb except by his son Muhammad; Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra was alone in narrating it."
"4755","4749 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Mundhir al-Warraq narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord is One, your father is one; no Arab has merit over a non-Arab, nor a non-Arab over an Arab, nor a red over a black, nor a black over a red, except by piety. This hadith was not narrated from al-Jurayri except by Abu al-Mundhir al-Warraq; Sahl ibn Uthman was alone in narrating it, and it is not narrated from Abu Sa'id except with this chain."
"4756","4750 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from Dawud ibn Shabur, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take much of sandals, for one of you remains mounted as long as he wears them. This hadith was not narrated from Dawud ibn Shabur except by Isma'il ibn Muslim, nor from Isma'il except by Ali ibn Hashim; Sahl ibn Uthman was alone in narrating it."
"4757","4751 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Azhar al-Naysaburi narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to me alone, saying: Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Ali and said: None loves you except a believer, and none hates you except a hypocrite; whoever loves you has loved me, and whoever hates you has hated me; my beloved is the beloved of Allah, and the one hateful to me is hateful to Allah; woe to whoever hates you after me. This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Razzaq except by Abu al-Azhar al-Naysaburi."
"4758","4752 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Madani narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Kharijah ibn Abdullah ibn Sulayman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, strengthen Islam with the more beloved of the two men to You: Umar ibn al-Khattab or Abu Jahl ibn Hisham - and the more beloved of them to Allah was Umar ibn al-Khattab. This hadith was not narrated from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah except by Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya."
"4759","4753 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ayyash, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays Duha four rak'ahs, and four before the first (Dhuhr) prayer, a house in Paradise is built for him thereby. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Burdah except by Abdullah ibn Ayyash, nor from Abdullah ibn Ayyash except by Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani; Sahl ibn Uthman was alone in narrating it."
"4760","4754 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Khalid, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cursed is the one who approaches women in their backsides. This hadith was not narrated from al-Ala except by Muslim ibn Khalid, nor from Muslim except by Ibn Abi Za'idah; Sahl ibn Uthman was alone in narrating it."
"4761","4755 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn Abu Mas'ud al-Sabuni al-Tustari narrated to us, saying: Abd al-A'la ibn Wasil ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Subayh al-Yashkuri narrated to us, saying: Mubarak ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: We used to travel with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when he saw a town he intended to enter, he would say: O Allah, bless us in it - three times - O Allah, grant us of its produce, make us beloved to its people, and make the righteous of its people beloved to us. This hadith was not narrated from Mubarak ibn Hassan except by Isma'il ibn Subayh."
"4762","4756 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Talhah al-Yarbu'i narrated to us, saying: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sharik, from Salim al-Aftas, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited {In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate}, the polytheists mocked him and said: Muhammad mentions the god of Yamamah - for Musaylimah used to call himself al-Rahman. When this verse was sent down, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded not to recite it aloud. This hadith was not narrated from Salim al-Aftas except by Sharik; Abbad ibn al-Awwam was alone in narrating it."
"4763","4757 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: Nasr ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Washsha narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn al-Hasan al-Anmati narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during his Hajj on the Day of Arafah, upon his she-camel al-Qaswa, delivering a sermon, and I heard him say: O people, I have left among you that which, if you hold to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and my progeny, my household. This hadith was not narrated from Ja'far ibn Muhammad except by Zayd ibn al-Hasan al-Anmati."
"4764","4758 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Mudrik narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: Sulayman al-Qaflani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept the prayer of one whose nose does not touch the ground. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Atiyyah except with this chain; al-Hasan ibn Mudrik was alone in narrating it."
"4765","4759 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: I found in my father's book, from Hafs ibn Umar al-Razi, from Abbad ibn Rashid, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind who said: Shu'bah said: from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked for a man to come to his family at night unexpectedly. This hadith was not narrated from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except by Abbad ibn Rashid; Hafs ibn Umar al-Razi was alone in narrating it, and we heard it only from al-Sabuni."
"4766","4760 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: I found in my father's book, from Hafs ibn Umar al-Razi, from Abu Hurrah who said: Ali ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered a sermon urging kinship, then said: Whoever has three daughters, caring for them, disciplining them and marrying them off, enters Paradise. Someone said: O Messenger of Allah, and two? He said: And two. Then Ali said: I did not lie against Muhammad, nor did Muhammad lie against Jabir, nor did Jabir lie against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith was not narrated from Abu Hurrah except by Hafs ibn Umar, and we heard it only from al-Sabuni."
"4767","4761 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, saying: Bistam ibn Muslim al-Awdhi narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Ata, from Jabir, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever owns land, let him cultivate it; if he cannot, let him grant its use, and not rent it out. Do not mix unripe dates with ripe dates, nor dates with raisins. A life-grant is permissible. This hadith was not narrated from Bistam ibn Muslim except by Muhammad ibn Bakr; Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i was alone in narrating it. And none narrates 'a life-grant is permissible' from Matar except Bistam."
"4768","4762 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: Zurayq ibn al-Sakht narrated to us, saying: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from Abu Malih ibn Usamah al-Hudhali, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed one of the hadds of Allah, so establish Allah's hadd upon me and purify me. He said: Did you not perform ablution well, purify yourself well, and witness the prayer with us just now? He said: Yes. He said: Go, for it is your expiation. This hadith is not narrated from Wathilah except with this chain; Hashim ibn al-Qasim was alone in narrating it."
"4769","4763 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: Zurayq ibn al-Sakht narrated to us, saying: Bakr ibn Khidash al-Kufi narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn al-Musayyib al-Bajali narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Ibn Buraydah who said: Buraydah informed me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no commander of ten except that he comes to Allah on the Day of Resurrection with his hand chained to his neck; if he was good, his chain is loosened, and if he was evil, chain is added to his chain. This hadith was not narrated from Isa ibn al-Musayyib except by Bakr ibn Khidash."
"4770","4764 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: Zurayq ibn al-Sakht narrated to us, saying: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn al-Musayyib al-Bajali narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi who said: Ka'b ibn Ujrah informed me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were seven: four of our freedmen and three of our Arabs, leaning our backs against his mosque. He said: What seated you? We said: We sat waiting for the prayer. He fell silent briefly, then turned to us and said: Do you know what your Lord says? We said: No. He said: Your Lord says: Whoever prays the prayer at its time, guards it, and does not neglect it belittling its right, has a covenant from Me that I admit him into Paradise; and whoever does not pray it at its time, does not guard it, and neglects it belittling its right, has no covenant from Me: if I wish I punish him, and if I wish I forgive him. This hadith was not narrated from Isa ibn al-Musayyib except by Hashim ibn al-Qasim."
"4771","4765 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: Zurayq ibn al-Sakht narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, saying: Affan ibn Jubayr al-Ta'i narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A day under a just ruler is better than sixty years of worship, and a hadd established in the land in truth is purer than forty mornings of rain. This hadith was not narrated from Ikrimah except by Affan ibn Jubayr; Ja'far ibn Awn was alone in narrating it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"4772","4766 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn Rashid al-Thaqafi narrated to us, saying: Anas ibn Sirin narrated to us, that they visited Anas ibn Malik on a Monday, and he invited them to lunch. Some of the people came forward and some held back, so he said: Perhaps you are Monday-fasters or Thursday-fasters - saying it three times? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast until they said he had no intention to break fast, and break fast until they said he had no intention to fast that year; and the most beloved fasting to him was in Sha'ban. This hadith was not narrated from Anas ibn Sirin except by Uthman ibn Rashid; Abd al-Samad was alone in narrating it."
"4773","4767 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn al-Dayf narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn al-Sakan al-Janadi narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Muslim narrated to me, from his father, from Ikrimah who said: Ibn Abbas was asked: Did Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) see his Lord, Mighty and Majestic? He said: Yes, he saw Him in the form of a youth with hair of pearls, as if his feet were in greenery. This hadith was not narrated from Amr ibn Muslim except by his son; Ishaq ibn al-Dayf was alone in narrating it."
"4774","4768 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, saying: al-Yaman ibn Nasr, the slave-trader, narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Sa'd al-Madani narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: I saw in a dream as though I were beneath a tree, and the tree was reciting {Sad}. When it reached the prostration it prostrated and said in its prostration: O Allah, write for me thereby a reward, remove from me thereby a burden, bring about for me thereby gratitude, and accept it from me as You accepted the prostration of Your servant Dawud. In the morning I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him of that. He said: Did you prostrate, O Abu Sa'id? I said: No. He said: You were more entitled to prostration than the tree. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Surah Sad until he reached the prostration, and said in his prostration what the tree had said in its prostration. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Sa'id except with this chain; al-Yaman ibn Nasr was alone in narrating it."
"4775","4769 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Yazid al-Ahwazi narrated to us, saying: Abu Hammam ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Marwan ibn Salim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, what about a man who slaughters and forgets to mention the name? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The name of Allah is upon the mouth of every Muslim."
"4776","4770 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Yazid al-Ahwazi narrated to us, saying: Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Marwan ibn Salim, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a sin is hidden it harms none but its doer, and when it appears and is not changed it harms the generality. These two hadiths were not narrated from al-Awza'i except by Marwan ibn Salim; Abu Hammam was alone in narrating them."
"4777","4771 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Sahl al-Mada'ini narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile my Companions; may Allah curse whoever reviles my Companions. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by Abu Asim; Ali ibn Sahl was alone in narrating it."
"4778","4772 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn Sahl al-Mada'ini narrated to us, saying: Shu'ayb ibn Harb narrated to us, saying: Mis'ar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Abu Awn Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah, from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah who said: I said to my father: O father, who is the best of this ummah after its Prophet? He said: Abu Bakr. I said: Then who? He said: Then Umar. Nothing prevented me from asking him about the third except fear that he would join Uthman in prayer (i.e. rank him third by praying for him). I said: What about you? He said: Your father is a man among the Muslims. This hadith was not narrated from Mis'ar except by Shu'ayb ibn Harb; Ali ibn Sahl was alone in narrating it."
"4779","4773 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi narrated to us, saying: Nahshal ibn Kathir narrated to us, saying: Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning or evening expedition in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it. This hadith was not narrated from al-A'mash except by Waki'; Nahshal ibn Kathir was alone in narrating it."
"4780","4774 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi narrated to us, saying: Jamil ibn al-Hasan al-Ataki narrated to us, saying: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Khalid ibn Maymun, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Abi Basir, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them in Fajr prayer, and when he turned he said: Is so-and-so present? Is so-and-so present? - for some hypocrites who had not attended the prayer. Then he said: The heaviest prayers upon them are these two prayers: Fajr and Isha; if they knew what is in them they would come to them crawling. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep to the front row, for it is like the row of the angels; if you knew what is in it you would hasten to it. He said: Your prayer with one man is purer than your prayer alone, your prayer with two men is purer than your prayer with one man, and the more the more beloved to Allah. This hadith was not narrated from Khalid ibn Maymun except by Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah; Abd al-A'la was alone in narrating it, and Ibn Shawdhab from Sa'id."
"4781","4775 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi narrated to us, saying: Sa'dan ibn Zakariyya al-Dawraqi narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Yahya al-Taymi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sa'id, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali; and al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ali; and Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, both saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is built upon three: the people of There is no god but Allah - do not declare them disbelievers for a sin, nor testify against them of polytheism; belief in the decrees, good and evil from Allah; and jihad continuing until the Day of Resurrection, since Allah sent Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until the last band of Muslims; the tyranny of a tyrant does not annul that, nor the justice of a just one. This hadith was not narrated from al-Thawri, al-Awza'i and Ibn Jurayj except by Isma'il ibn Yahya al-Taymi."
"4782","4776 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi narrated to us, saying: Sa'dan ibn Zakariyya al-Dawraqi narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Yahya al-Taymi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When a man adorns himself for a deed of the Hereafter while neither intending it nor seeking it, he is cursed in the heavens and the earths. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Ibn Abi Dhi'b; Isma'il ibn Yahya was alone in narrating it."
"4783","4777 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad narrated to us, saying: Sa'dan ibn Zakariyya al-Dawraqi narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Umar ibn al-Khattab who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from rulers of hardship who drive my ummah to wrongdoing. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Hanifah except by Isma'il ibn Yahya."
"4784","4778 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that Hamzah al-Aslami said: O Messenger of Allah, I fast continuously without breaking - shall I fast while traveling? He said: If you wish, fast; if you wish, break fast."
"4785","4779 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Khallad al-Dawraqi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever revives a dead land has reward in it, and whatever wild animals eat of it is charity for him. These two hadiths were not narrated from Ayyub except by Abd al-Wahhab."
"4786","Abdur-Rahman ibn Ziyad Abu Mas'ud al-Kinani al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Abda ibn Abdillah al-Khuza'i as-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Abu al-Ash'ath as-San'ani, from Aws ibn Aws ath-Thaqafi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the best of your days is Friday; on it Adam was created, on it he was taken, on it is the blowing and on it is the swoon, so send much salat upon me on it, for your salat upon me is presented to me. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will our salat be presented to you when you have decayed? He said, they say: you have rotted. He said: Indeed Allah has forbidden the earth to consume the bodies of the Prophets. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jabir except Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi."
"4787","Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Muthanna ibn Muta' ibn Isa ibn Muta' ibn Ziyada ibn Muslim ibn Mas'ud ibn ad-Dahhak ibn Jabir ibn Adi ibn Arsh ibn Jadila ibn Lakhm Abu Mas'ud al-Lakhmi narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna narrated to me, from his father Muta', from his father Isa, from his father Muta', from his father Ziyada, from his grandfather Mas'ud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Muta' and said to him: O Muta', you are obeyed among your people; and he mounted him on a piebald horse and gave him the banner, and said to him: O Muta', go to your companions; whoever enters under this banner of mine is safe from punishment. This hadith is not narrated from Mas'ud ibn ad-Dahhak except with this chain; our shaykh Abdur-Rahman is alone in it."
"4788","Abdur-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Rushdin al-Misri narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Hashimi the judge narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Jari narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged by an oath along with a witness. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Sa'id except with this chain; Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid is alone in it."
"4789","Ubayd ibn Ghannam ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath ibn Talq ibn Mu'awiya an-Nakha'i narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah; Sharik said: I think it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Is there not among you one who can recite a third of the Qur'an in a night? They said: Who can bear this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Does not one of you recite Say: He is Allah, the One, for it equals a third of the Qur'an. No one connected this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Sharik."
"4790","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id and Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'isha, who said: I missed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I followed him to the graveyard, and he said: Peace be upon you, O abode of a believing people; you are our forerunners. Then he turned to me and saw me and said: Woe to her, if she could she would have done it. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id and Asim ibn Ubaydillah except Sharik."
"4791","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Abdillah al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, from Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym, from Zayd ibn Abi al-Attab, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best house among the Muslims is a house in which there is an orphan who is treated well, and the worst house among the Muslims is a house in which there is an orphan who is treated badly. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hurayra except Ibn Abi al-Attab; Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub is alone in it."
"4792","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Makhlad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Mukharrimi, from Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Akhnasi, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no one who goes out except that at his door are two banners: a banner in the hand of an angel and a banner in the hand of a devil. If he goes out for what Allah loves, the angel follows him with his banner, and he remains under the angel's banner until he returns to his house; and if he goes out for what angers Allah, the devil follows him with his banner, and he remains under the devil's banner until he returns. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayra except with this chain; Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Akhnasi is alone in it."
"4793","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Makhlad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad az-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no good in trade except for one who does not praise what he sells, does not dispraise what he buys, earns lawfully, spends it where due, and keeps oaths out of it. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Umar ibn Rashid; Abu Ahmad az-Zubayri is alone in it."
"4794","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra, that Iblis wailed when the Opening of the Book was revealed, and it was revealed in Madina. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Abu al-Ahwas; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba is alone in it."
"4795","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Ata, meaning Ya'qub, from his father, in what Abu Bakr narrates from Jabir ibn Abdillah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fresh dates for dry dates and grapes for raisins, and he permitted araya. No one narrated this hadith from Ya'qub ibn Ata except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Ali ibn Hakim is alone in it."
"4796","Ubayd ibn Kathir at-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The neighbor has most right to his adjoining property. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi' except Ibn Abi Layla; Muhammad ibn Imran and al-Hasan ibn Abd ar-Rahim ibn Abi Layla are alone in it."
"4797","Ubayd ibn Kathir at-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Furat ibn Mahbub narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Umara ibn Umayr, from Abu Ma'mar, from Abu Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever guides to good, he has the like of the reward of its doer. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash, from Umara, except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; and ath-Thawri and others narrated it from al-A'mash, from Abu Amr ash-Shaybani, from Abu Mas'ud."
"4798","Ubayd ibn Kathir at-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salim ibn Abi Hafsa narrated to us, from Hashim ibn al-Barid, from Bayan Abu Bishr, from Zadham, from Abdullah, who said: I recited seventy suras to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I completed the Qur'an under the best of people, Ali ibn Abi Talib. No one narrated this hadith from Bayan except Hashim ibn al-Barid, nor from Hashim except Yahya ibn Salim; Muhammad ibn al-Junayd is alone in it."
"4799","Ubayd ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Dubays narrated to us, he said: Ubayda ibn al-Aswad al-Hamdani narrated to us, from al-Qasim, from al-Walid, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek protection for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, saying: I seek protection for you two by the perfect words of Allah from every devil and vermin, and from every harmful eye. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim except Ubayda; Abdur-Rahman ibn Dubays is alone in it."
"4800","Ubayd ibn Kathir at-Tammar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Ibrahim as-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Hamza ibn Imran ibn Muslim, from Ziyad ibn Khaythama, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Hani, from Ali, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Ammar asked permission, and he said: Welcome to the good, perfumed one. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Khaythama except Hamza ibn Imran ibn Muslim, and Hamza ibn Imran did not narrate any hadith with a chain except this one."
